s the United States Representative for Idaho 's 1st congressional district from 2001 to 2007", "context_len": 27}}}, "muskrat": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "They traded beaver , deer , marten , raccoon , fox , otter , and muskrat", "context_len": 16}}}, "metal": {"freq": 142, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 9, "context": "Before this layer sets , terrazzo workers partially embed metal divider strips in the concrete wherever there is to be a joint or change of color in the terrazzo", "context_len": 29}, "NOUN": {"freq": 134, "word_index": 24, "context": "Unlike numismatic coins , a bullion coin is a coin , new or old , that is bought only for the price of the metal it is made of , not for its condition , age or any other value , british gold sovereigns are a common historic bullion coin , and most countries produce a coin meant solely for bullion purposes in different weights , e", "context_len": 67}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "Silver is used widely in mission-critical applications as electrical contacts , and is also used in photography ( because silver nitrate reverts to metal on exposure to light ) , agriculture , medicine , audiophile and scientific applications", "context_len": 38}}}, "tools": {"freq": 32, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 32, "word_index": 12, "context": "In the past , there were major United Nations ' human rights tools like the Universal Declaration on Human Rights , the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights or International Covenant on Economic , Social and Cultural Rights", "context_len": 39}}}, "cloths": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "The Odawa got metal tools , cloths , weapons , jewelry and alcohol in return", "context_len": 15}}}, "weapons": {"freq": 72, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 72, "word_index": 22, "context": "The International Atomic Energy Agency ( IAEA ) has reported numerous times that there is no evidence that Iran is developing nuclear weapons , however , it also says that it can not say for sure that Iran is not doing so in secret", "context_len": 44}}}, "jewelry": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 8, "context": "After photos of Mendoza modeling naked for a jewelry firm surfaced , officials from the Miss Universe Organization decided against penalizing her , saying that the candid photos were not pornographic but `` artistic in nature , and they do n't have an ounce of pornographic content to them", "context_len": 49}}}, "alcohol": {"freq": 24, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 21, "word_index": 33, "context": "He did not like to eat vegetables but liked beef , pork and chicken , and daily ate toffee and drank a glass of milk and the occasional apple juice and only drank alcohol in moderation , which he believed as the secrets to a long life", "context_len": 47}, "VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "Drunkards were `` slaves '' to alcohol , workers were `` slaves '' to the factory owners , and women were `` slaves '' to men", "context_len": 26}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Police would arrest anyone who was found making or selling alcohol illegally", "context_len": 12}}}, "wars": {"freq": 26, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 26, "word_index": 21, "context": "The effect is well-documented for the period of the First and Second World War , but it also applies to other wars , such as the Philippine\u2013American War , the Vietnam War , the Korean War or the Occupation of Japan", "context_len": 41}}}, "trading": {"freq": 39, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 34, "word_index": 12, "context": ") Also , there is another special type of Pok\u00e9mon in the trading card game called `` Delta Species '' Pok\u00e9mon , which have types that are different than typical cards , like an Electric-type Charmander , who is usually Fire-type", "context_len": 41}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 15, "context": "However , most Native Americans left the travelers alone , or even helped them by trading with them and helping them cross rivers in canoes", "context_len": 25}}}, "powerful": {"freq": 98, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 98, "word_index": 72, "context": "The Second Mexican Empire ( ) , Officially the Mexican Empire ( ) , was a Constitutional Monarchy and Client state of the Second French Empire in Mexico , it was ruled by Maximilian of Habsburg who ruled as `` Maximilian I of Mexico '' and his wife `` Charlotte of Mexico '' , it was established during the Second French intervention in Mexico as a client state to compete with the powerful United States , This is nothing related to the First Mexican Empire of Agust\u00edn I", "context_len": 88}}}, "diseases": {"freq": 41, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 40, "word_index": 0, "context": "Diseases that can be infected through airborne transmission may be viruses , bacteria , or fungi , and they may be spread through breathing , talking , coughing , sneezing , raising of dust , spraying of liquids or even flushing toilets", "context_len": 42}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "According to the beliefs of the fishermen of the Karang Island , diseases with unexplainable causes are caused by gods and goddesses", "context_len": 22}}}, "natives": {"freq": 18, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 18, "word_index": 39, "context": "Throughout the temple texts , Hatshepsut `` maintains the fiction that her envoy '' Chancellor Nehsi , who is mentioned as the head of the expedition , had travelled to Punt `` in order to extract tribute from the natives '' who admit their allegiance to the Egyptian pharaoh", "context_len": 49}}}, "immune": {"freq": 33, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 14, "word_index": 55, "context": "In response , then Coalition Treasurer Peter Costello 's removed the pillar status of the two insurers ( National Mutual had by that time already been acquired by France 's AXA ) , but the ban on mergers of the remaining four banks was retained , with the rider that none of them were considered immune from foreign takeover", "context_len": 59}, "NOUN": {"freq": 19, "word_index": 34, "context": "The evolution of the MHC polymorphism means that a population will not succumb to a new pathogen or a mutated one , because at least some individuals will be able to develop an adequate immune response to defeat the pathogen", "context_len": 40}}}, "attacked": {"freq": 82, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 79, "word_index": 26, "context": "It is likely that because the pilots had been warned of the World Trade Center attacks and to beware of cockpit intrusion , when the hijackers attacked them , they purposely pressed on the talk button of the radio microphone , so sounds of the struggle in the cockpit will be heard by FAA ground controllers and by pilots of planes on the same radio frequency", "context_len": 66}, "UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 9, "context": "On Flight 11 , Satam al-Suqami in seat 10B attacked passenger Daniel Lewin , who was seated directly in front of him in 9B", "context_len": 24}}}, "surrendered": {"freq": 10, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 31, "context": "In one battle , the cutter `` Surveyor '' put up such a fight against the larger British frigate `` HMS Narcissus '' , that when the `` Surveyor '' finally surrendered , The British Captain returned the sword of the American captain in recognition of his bravery", "context_len": 48}}}, "handed": {"freq": 13, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 13, "word_index": 7, "context": "In 2007 , the government of Pakistan handed over port operations to PSA Singapore for 25 years , and gave it the status of a Tax Free Port for the following 40 years", "context_len": 33}}}, "negotiations": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 13, "context": "IFPRI also analyzes agricultural market reforms , trade policy , World Trade Organization negotiations in the context of agriculture , institutional effectiveness , crop and income diversification , postharvest activity , and agroindustry", "context_len": 33}}}, "ate": {"freq": 15, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 33, "context": "Mephibosheth bowed down and cried , `` What is your servant , that you should notice a dead dog like me ? '' From then on , Mephibosheth lived in Jerusalem and always ate at the king 's table like one of David 's sons", "context_len": 45}, "NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 17, "context": "He did not like to eat vegetables but liked beef , pork and chicken , and daily ate toffee and drank a glass of milk and the occasional apple juice and only drank alcohol in moderation , which he believed as the secrets to a long life", "context_len": 47}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "They found the island 's only known drinkable water-source \u2013 a brackish spring on the north shore , exposed at half tide \u2013 and ate fish , birds , eggs , crabs and peppergrass , but they had largely exhausted the available food within a week", "context_len": 46}}}, "town": {"freq": 682, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 682, "word_index": 15, "context": "Though palm trees and desert scenery are seen in shots of the local region and town throughout the show , indicating a location in the Western United States , it is never revealed which state the show is set in ( except for Francis 's whereabouts in early seasons , such as his military school in Alabama and his job in Alaska )", "context_len": 63}}}, "events": {"freq": 194, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 194, "word_index": 4, "context": "One month after the events of `` '' ( 2016 ) , Buck is back in the Lost World and continues protecting the place from rogue dinosaurs until his old nemesis Orson , a talking dwarf Triceratop with a big brain , comes back for revenge and wants to rule the Lost World , getting ride of all mammals in it and avoiding every mammal to enter in there", "context_len": 69}}}, "increased": {"freq": 73, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 64, "word_index": 8, "context": "In 2016 , Milenio Televisi\u00f3n 's open signal increased when it was authorized to be transmitted as part of the multiprogramming of the main channel in the cities of : Torre\u00f3n , Le\u00f3n , Nuevo Laredo , Ciudad Victoria , Tampico and Matamoros", "context_len": 43}, "UNK": {"freq": 9, "word_index": 7, "context": "The Security Statute gave the military an increased degree of freedom of action , especially in urban areas , to detain , interrogate and eventually judge suspected guerrillas or their collaborators before military tribunals", "context_len": 34}}}, "tension": {"freq": 50, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 50, "word_index": 24, "context": "The liquid mass flattens out because that brings as much of the mercury to as low a level as possible , but the surface tension , at the same time , is acting to reduce the total surface area", "context_len": 39}}}, "eventually": {"freq": 111, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 111, "word_index": 66, "context": "By the 3rd century Jews of the diaspora ( Jewish people outside of their country ) were speaking Greek , and soon afterwards Hebrew was no longer used as a first language - for over sixteen centuries being used almost only as a liturgical language ( for prayer ) until revived as a spoken language by Eliezer Ben-Yehuda in the Palestine of the late 1880s and eventually becoming the official language of the state of Israel", "context_len": 76}}}, "chief": {"freq": 137, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 32, "word_index": 10, "context": "Mahmoud Refaat led the presidential campaign of former Egyptian army chief of staff Lieutenant General Sami Anan from abroad and played a role in covering all the international media news of the arrest of General Sami Anan , which he explained in several televised meetings that he did so for fear of assassination of Lieutenant General Sami Anan", "context_len": 58}, "UNK": {"freq": 105, "word_index": 34, "context": "Andy 's toys are welcomed by the numerous toys at Sunnyside , and given a tour of the seemingly perfect play-settin