 an underground stem of a plant , such as the potato , with buds from which new plant shoots ( stems and young leaves of a new plant ) grow", "context_len": 37}}}, "leadership": {"freq": 54, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 54, "word_index": 14, "context": "In September 2015 , she supported Jeremy Corbyn 's campaign in the Labour Party leadership election , In 2016 , Church along with many other celebrities , toured the UK to support Corbyn 's bid to become Prime Minister , and in March 2016 , performed at a socialist fundraising event in Edinburgh for Corbyn", "context_len": 55}}}, "contributions": {"freq": 30, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 30, "word_index": 14, "context": "Among the most striking recent accomplishments of Todor\u010devi\u0107 ( and co-authors ) are major contributions to the von Neumann and Maharam problems on Boolean algebras , the theory of non-separable Banach spaces , including the solution of an old problem of Davis and Johnson , the solution of a long-standing problem of Laver , and the development of a duality theory relating finite Ramsey theory and topological dynamics", "context_len": 68}}}, "cabinet": {"freq": 37, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 36, "word_index": 48, "context": "On February 7 , 2017 , DeVos was confirmed by the Senate by a 51\u201350 margin , with Vice President Mike Pence breaking the tie in favor of DeVos 's nomination ; it was the first time a vice president had done so for the appointment of a cabinet nominee", "context_len": 50}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Oliart was a cabinet member during the Adolfo Su\u00e1rez and Leopoldo Calvo-Sotelo governments", "context_len": 13}}}, "art": {"freq": 181, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 163, "word_index": 29, "context": "He contributed fundamentals to many fields of visual arts ( painting , sculpture , movie , industrial design , graphic design ) in modernism , futurism , and concrete art , and in non visual arts ( literature , poetry ) with his research on games , didactic method , movement , tactile learning , kinesthetic learning , and creativity", "context_len": 60}, "UNK": {"freq": 15, "word_index": 36, "context": "Georges Braque ( Argenteuil , 13 May 1882 \u2013 Paris , 31 August 1963 ) was a major 20th century French painter , collagist , printmaker and sculptor who , with Pablo Picasso , developed the art movement known as Cubism", "context_len": 41}, "VERB": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 5, "context": "They used the terms `` art nude '' and `` figurenude '' from painting to avoid suggestions that their works were meant to be erotica or pornography", "context_len": 27}}}, "pixel": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "His video game contributions began with arcade cabinet art , then pixel art design as in the arcade `` Sheriff '' ( 1979 ) , full game codevelopment roles as in the arcade `` Radar Scope '' ( 1980 ) , ukreplicawatch", "context_len": 42}, "NOUN": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 13, "context": "When the mirror spends more time reflecting light through the lens , the pixel is lighter", "context_len": 16}}}, "phenomenal": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "is primary concept and development roles as in Nintendo 's first phenomenal hit `` Donkey Kong '' ( 1981 ) , and his first console-only game `` Devil World '' ( 1984 )", "context_len": 33}}}, "designers": {"freq": 14, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 14, "word_index": 37, "context": "High Fashion '' ( September 1986 ) feature article Karl Davis : A New , Up-and-Coming Designer Who Enjoys Dressing Up , columnist Yoko Hamada wrote concerning Davis \u2019 s stylish way of dressing that Although many designers dress well , it hard to find someone who loves dressing up as much as Karl", "context_len": 54}}}, "sole": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 25, "context": "Meitei script ( ) or Meetei script ( ) is an abugida used for Meitei language ( officially known as Manipuri language ) , the sole official language , the lingua franca and the predominantly spoken tongue of the Indian state of Manipur", "context_len": 43}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 22, "context": "Trans World Airlines , United Airlines , and finally Continental Airlines left to serve more profitable routes , leaving US Airways the sole carrier", "context_len": 24}}}, "dictatorship": {"freq": 10, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 31, "context": "However , the proof that there was a fraud is not found , so far and people believes that Tatmadaw made the coup because the generals wants to restart the military dictatorship which ended about 10 years ago", "context_len": 38}}}, "imprisoned": {"freq": 18, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 18, "word_index": 21, "context": "Tito 's repression involved many of the his old friends such as Milovan Dilas and Vladimir Dedijer , who were both imprisoned but later wrote several books with gross accusations against him ; with criticism heaped on Tito 's lustful lifestyle : by 1974 he had 32 official residences , one of the ten richest men in the Balkans , `` a communist who lived like a king ''", "context_len": 69}}}, "island": {"freq": 343, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 343, "word_index": 47, "context": "When referring specifically to the lower Manhattan business district such as Wall Street and its immediate environs , the northern border is commonly designated by thoroughfares approximately a mile-and-a-half ( 3 km ) south of 14th Street and a mile ( 2 km ) north of the island 's southern tip : Chambers Street from near the Hudson east to the Brooklyn Bridge entrances and overpass", "context_len": 66}}}, "subversive": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 20, "context": "Austria-Hungary 's government did not directly accuse Serbia for the assassination but for `` doing nothing to suppress '' the subversive anti-Austro-Hungarian movement in Serbia which grew beyond Serbia 's borders and which was responsible for acts of terrorism , assassination attempts and murders", "context_len": 44}}}, "ally": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 43, "context": "Tecumseh ( ; March 1768 \u2013 October 5 , 1813 ) was a Native American leader of the Shawnee and a large tribal confederacy ( known as Tecumseh 's Confederacy ) which opposed the United States during Tecumseh 's War and became an ally of Britain in the War of 1812", "context_len": 51}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "The concept dates from Anglo-Saxon times , when a church could ally itself with the monarch and therefore not be subject to the bishop of the area", "context_len": 27}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Ally McBeal is an American TV show that was on air from September 8 , 1997 , to May 20 , 2002 , by the Fox Channel", "context_len": 27}}}, "prominent": {"freq": 38, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 36, "word_index": 3, "context": "He has received prominent bullfighters like Julian L\u00f3pez `` El Juli '' , Francisco Rivera Ord\u00f3\u00f1ez , Juan Jos\u00e9 `` Morante de la Puebla '' , Miguel \u00c1ngel Perera , Enrique Ponce , Francisco Rivera `` Paquirr\u00ed '' , P\u00e1lomo Lin\u00e1res , Javier Conde , Manuel B\u00e9nitez `` El Cordob\u00e9s '' , Jos\u00e9 Mar\u00eda Manzanares , Antonio Barrera , Paquito Perlaza , Leonardo B\u00e9nitez , Luis Bolivar , David Fandila `` El Fandi '' , Mary Paz Vega , Morenito de Maracay , Nerio Ramirez `` El Tovare\u00f1o '' , Rafael Orellana , C\u00e9sar Vanegas , C\u00e9sar Faraco , Eduardo Valenzuela , among others", "context_len": 104}, "NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 13, "context": "Within his alma-mater ( Leiden University ) educational environment , he became a prominent and ultimate professor for Acehnese and Malay literature , and also gave special classes in the Acehnese language", "context_len": 32}}}, "prisons": {"freq": 12, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 12, "word_index": 6, "context": "She wants there to be no prisons or police because she believes that the US prison system is more like a new form of slavery than a criminal justice system", "context_len": 30}}}, "activists": {"freq": 27, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 27, "word_index": 8, "context": "Beginning in the 1980s , many anti-nuclear power activists began shifting their interest , by joining a rapidly growing nuclear freeze movement , and the primary concern about nuclear hazards in the USA changed from the problems of nuclear power plants to the prospects of nuclear war", "context_len": 47}}}, "exiled": {"freq": 12, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 20, "context": "Under Yezhov , the purges reached their height , with roughly half of the Soviet political and military establishment being exiled or shot , along with hundreds of thousands of others , suspected of disloyalty or wrecking", "context_len": 37}, "UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 3, "context": "Khalil is an exiled Bangladeshi journalist living in Sweden", "context_len": 9}}}, "deportations": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "Between the 1940s and 1960s Villanueva spent his time in between Peruvian prisons and deportations to Chile and Argentina", "context_len": 19}}}, "amnesty": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 7, "context": "In late 1961 , before a general amnesty was granted to members of APRA , Villanueva entered Peru secretly", "context_len": 19}}}, "organizing": {"freq": 12, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 12, "word_index": 28, "context": "The main aims of the NSCA , declared in its Founding Act and Statute , include assembling Serbian clarinetists interested in researching the clarinet and clarinet literature , organizing clarinet-related events , and collaborating with foreign clarinetists and clarinet associations", "context_len": 40}}}, "preparation": {"freq": 48, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 48, "word_index": 19, "context": "An exhibition game ( also known as simply exhibition , or a demonstration event , a friendly , a preparation ma