 resources instead of someone else 's )", "context_len": 64}}}, "disagreements": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 12, "context": "Toward the end of his professional career , he began to have disagreements with staff members ; some days Garroway would disappear in the middle of the `` Today '' broadcast , leaving colleagues to finish the live program", "context_len": 39}}}, "liked": {"freq": 68, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 67, "word_index": 8, "context": "He did not like to eat vegetables but liked beef , pork and chicken , and daily ate toffee and drank a glass of milk and the occasional apple juice and only drank alcohol in moderation , which he believed as the secrets to a long life", "context_len": 47}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "On the Edison Media Research and Pinnacle Media Worldwide lists , the song was both liked and disliked", "context_len": 18}}}, "perpetrators": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "The perpetrators of the attacks were called bushwhackers", "context_len": 8}}}, "bushwhackers": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 7, "context": "The historian Albert Castel says that the bushwhackers under Quantrill also wanted to steal , but revenge was their main reason", "context_len": 21}}}, "bushwhacking": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "The term `` bushwhacking '' is still in use today to describe ambushes done with the goal of attrition", "context_len": 19}}}, "ambushes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "The term `` bushwhacking '' is still in use today to describe ambushes done with the goal of attrition", "context_len": 19}}}, "attrition": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "The term `` bushwhacking '' is still in use today to describe ambushes done with the goal of attrition", "context_len": 19}}}, "mighty": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"UNK": {"fre