q": 18, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 18, "word_index": 23, "context": "Lisa Schwarzbaum of `` Entertainment Weekly '' gave the movie a score of a `` B , '' saying that `` There are moments of real funniness in this smarter-than-anticipated goof-fest", "context_len": 31}}}, "estimation": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 6, "context": "According to the ( 2021 ) estimation , the West Bengal state has over 31,144,763 Muslims , who form 30 % of the state 's population", "context_len": 26}}}, "parameters": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 15, "context": "With the help of the Van der Waals 's equation of state , the critical-point parameters of gases could be accurately predicted from thermodynamic measurements made at much higher temperatures", "context_len": 30}}}, "expressed": {"freq": 23, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 23, "word_index": 11, "context": "The result is that the more microscopic Amp\u00e8re 's law , expressed in terms of B and the microscopic current ( which includes free , magnetization and polarization currents ) , is sometimes put into the equivalent form below in terms of H and the free current only", "context_len": 48}}}, "sample": {"freq": 23, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 20, "word_index": 27, "context": "The nominees for the 32nd People 's Choice Awards were picked by web research company Knowledge Networks , which took what it described as a nationally representative sample of men and women ages 18 to 54 , with and without Internet access , to come up with the nominees after being presented with a list of candidates determined by national ratings averages , box office grosses and album sales , and they had the option to write in their favorites", "context_len": 80}, "UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "be the `` j '' -th sample moment , an estimate of formula 12", "context_len": 14}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "For example , if we were interested in crows , then we would sample the set of crows which is of interest", "context_len": 22}}}, "leads": {"freq": 45, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 40, "word_index": 17, "context": "The movie is about a graduate student in Chicago finishing a thesis on urban legends , which leads her to the legend of `` Candyman '' , the ghost of an artist and son of a slave who was murdered in the late 19th century", "context_len": 45}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 10, "context": "It was found in very old river beds called `` leads '' which had been buried for thousands of years", "context_len": 20}}}, "values": {"freq": 52, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 52, "word_index": 55, "context": "`` Pr\u00eat '' ( May 1986 ) said Davis was beginning to shake up the New York fashion scene with his elegant , dramatic cuts and sophisticated sense of style , that his designs were Inspired by the looks of Dior , Balenciaga and Chanel ; and that he took a modern approach to the values and attitudes of Haute Couture and reinvented them for a new , younger generation", "context_len": 70}}}, "moment": {"freq": 46, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 46, "word_index": 68, "context": "By convention , the direction of the vector area is given by the right hand grip rule ( curling the fingers of one 's right hand in the direction of the current around the loop , when the palm of the hand is `` touching '' the loop 's outer edge , and the straight thumb indicates the direction of the vector area and thus of the magnetic moment )", "context_len": 70}}}, "denoted": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 48, "context": "The word was coined by scientist Andreas von Antropoff in 1926 ( before the discovery of the neutron ) for the hypothetical `` element of atomic number zero '' ( with zero protons in its nucleus ) that he placed at the start of the periodic table ( denoted by dash , no element symbol )", "context_len": 56}}}, "solution": {"freq": 45, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 45, "word_index": 19, "context": "People do n't know h