pose of the mission ) , to New Zealand and to the east coast of Australia , where Cook mapped the coastline and made landfall at Botany Bay and at Endeavour River ( near modern Cooktown ) in Queensland , where they spent seven weeks ashore while the ship was repaired after damage on the Great Barrier Reef", "context_len": 74}}}, "beach": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 42, "context": "There is only one known source of drinking water on the island : a brackish spring on the north shore exposed at half tide , rising from a crevice in flat rock , large surfaces of which compose the face of the beach", "context_len": 43}}}, "waves": {"freq": 54, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 53, "word_index": 34, "context": "In October 1859 John Brown 's raid on the Harpers Ferry Armory in what is now Harpers Ferry , West Virginia ( at the time part of the state of Virginia ) sent shock waves through the South", "context_len": 38}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "The sun waves radiate the short-wave radiation", "context_len": 7}}}, "drift": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 19, "context": "In the 2000s , the role of gene duplication , the extent of adaptive molecular evolution versus neutral genetic drift , and the identification of molecular changes responsible for various human characteristics especially those pertaining to infection , disease , and cognition", "context_len": 42}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "The spectators drift away", "context_len": 4}}}, "collects": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 3, "context": "When a player collects a weapon or power-up , it will appear in a box at the top of the screen", "context_len": 21}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "When it rains , fresh water collects in the valleys between sand dunes", "context_len": 13}}}, "flag": {"freq": 67, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 66, "word_index": 35, "context": "In August 1937 , HMS Le