fferson and the Slave Power '' , historian Garry Wills wrote , the South was not demanding slave representation to achieve a near-parity at the moment , but as a way of achieving majority control in the immediately foreseeable future", "context_len": 47}}}, "abolitionists": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 18, "context": "Slave Power , also called the Slave Power conspiracy and Slaveocracy , was a term first used by abolitionists in 1839 and was in common use by the 1850s", "context_len": 29}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "When open war broke out in the Kansas Territory ( called Bleeding Kansas ) , Southern slaveholders , Northern abolitionists and Free-soilers flooded into Kansas", "context_len": 25}}}, "betrayal": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "The betrayal of James and Lily Potter , the murder of Peter Pettigrew and 12 muggles with an unknown curse", "context_len": 20}}}, "debating": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 6, "context": "Recently , with the Anglican Church debating if female clergymen should be allowed , some Anglo-Catholics , such as Bishop Burnham , Bishop Newton and sixty priests left the Church and converted to Rome in protest , as they do not believe female bishops or female priests should be allowed", "context_len": 50}}}, "mentions": {"freq": 16, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 9, "word_index": 27, "context": "For example , `` One Hundred Years of Progress : The Centennial History of Anna , Illinois , '' although more than 400 pages long , never mentions Anna 's 1909 expulsion of African Americans , the sundown signs at the northern and southern city limits in 1954 , or anything else about race", "context_len": 54}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 2, "context": "Herodotus , mentions the word `` Spaka '' ( `` Dog '' , still present in current Iranian languages such as tat and talysh , and different from Persian )", "context_len": 30}}}, "synagogue": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "The synagogue was established on 15 April 1840", "context_len": 8}}}, "sanctuary": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 19, "context": "The name traces back to Plato 's school of philosophy , founded about 385 BC at Akademia , a sanctuary of Athena , the goddess of wisdom , north of Athens , Greece", "context_len": 33}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "In the North , free black communities provided runaway slaves with sanctuary and hid them from the hired kidnappers searching for them", "context_len": 22}}}, "premises": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 5, "context": "The argument could have true premises , but still have a false conclusion", "context_len": 13}}}, "emigrated": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 15, "context": "He was born in New York City to William and Marie Fazzin , who had emigrated to the United States from Austria", "context_len": 22}}}, "peasant": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 15, "context": "Villein land could not be abandoned , at least not as long as every fleeing peasant was likely to starve to death ; nor could they be passed to a third party without the lord 's permission , and the customary payment", "context_len": 42}, "UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 23, "context": "The effect of circumstances on manorial economy is complex and at times contradictory : upland conditions have been seen as tending to preserve peasant freedoms ( livestock husbandry is less labour-intensive and therefore less demanding of villein services ) ; on the other hand , some such areas of Europe have been said to show some of the most oppressive manorial conditions , while lowland eastern England is credited with an exceptionally large free peasantry , in part a legacy of Scandinavian settlement", "context_len": 83}}}, "implemented": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq":