ce problem turn out to be useful in many other problems in general topology , writing `` this is so because Ramsey-type theorems are basic and so much needed in many parts of mathematics and ( S ) and ( L ) happen to be Ramsey-type properties of the uncountable most often needed by the topologist ''", "context_len": 62}}}, "subsets": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 34, "context": "He made major contributions to the study of S- and L-spaces in topology , proved a remarkable classification theorem for transitive relations on the first uncountable ordinal , made a deep study of compact subsets of the Baire class 1 functions thus continuing work of Bourgain , Fremlin , Talagrand , and others in Banach space theory", "context_len": 57}}}, "larson": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Larson he completed the solution of Katetov \u2019 s old compact spaces metrization problem", "context_len": 14}}}, "algebras": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 24, "context": "Among the most striking recent accomplishments of Todor\u010devi\u0107 ( and co-authors ) are major contributions to the von Neumann and Maharam problems on Boolean algebras , the theory of non-separable Banach spaces , including the solution of an old problem of Davis and Johnson , the solution of a long-standing problem of Laver , and the development of a duality theory relating finite Ramsey theory and topological dynamics", "context_len": 68}}}, "duality": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 59, "context": "Among the most striking recent accomplishments of Todor\u010devi\u0107 ( and co-authors ) are major contributions to the von Neumann and Maharam problems on Boolean algebras , the theory of non-separable Banach spaces , including the solution of an old problem of Davis and Johnson , the solution of a long-standing problem of Laver , and the development of a duality theory relating finite Ramsey theory and topological dynamics", "context_len": 68}}}, "finite": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 62, "context": "Among the most striking recent accomplishments of Todor\u010devi\u0107 ( and co-authors ) are major contributions to the von Neumann and Maharam problems on Boolean algebras , the theory of non-separable Banach spaces , including the solution of an old problem of Davis and Johnson , the solution of a long-standing problem of Laver , and the development of a duality theory relating finite Ramsey theory and topological dynamics", "context_len": 68}}}, "dynamics": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 67, "context": "Among the most striking recent accomplishments of Todor\u010devi\u0107 ( and co-authors ) are major contributions to the von Neumann and Maharam problems on Boolean algebras , the theory of non-separable Banach spaces , including the solution of an old problem of Davis and Johnson , the solution of a long-standing problem of Laver , and the development of a duality theory relating finite Ramsey theory and topological dynamics", "context_len": 68}}}, "ordinals": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 21, "context": "Further , Todor\u010devi\u0107 is known for his the side-condition method in set-theoretic forcing , the invention and development of walks on ordinals and their characteristics , and other research that bridge between different areas of mathematics", "context_len": 36}}}, "continuum": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 16, "context": "He constructed a model of formula 1 in a way to allow him to make the continuum any regular cardinal and derived a variety of topological consequences of formula 2 Here formula 3 is an abbreviation for Martin 's Axiom and formula 4\u2013 for weak Kurepa Hypothesis", "context_len": 47}}}, "rigid": {"freq": 9, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 10, "context": "The flexible rules about baseball fields ( aside from the rigid rules of sizes of basepaths and pitcher 's mound ) allow ballparks to have their own character and quirks", "context_len": 30}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "On the other hand , gram-negative bacteria have thin , insignificant peptidoglycan layers , so they do need rigid cell walls for support and protection", "context_len": 25}}}, "consistency": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 8, "context": "Usually , lentils are boiled to a stew-like consistency with vegetables and then seasoned with a mixture of spices to make many side dishes such as sambar , rasam and dal , which are usually served over rice and roti", "context_len": 40}}}, "countable": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "Mathematicians say that this is the branch of mathematics dealing with countable sets ( sets that have the same cardinality as subsets of the natural numbers , including rational numbers but not real numbers )", "context_len": 35}}}, "combinatorial": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "He gave a survey of work on trees from combinatorial and set-theoretic perspectives , in the 1980s", "context_len": 17}}}, "perspectives": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "He gave a survey of work on trees from combinatorial and set-theoretic perspectives , in the 1980s", "context_len": 17}}}, "possibilities": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 8, "context": ", and continued this work on exploring consistent possibilities for various types of trees , looking for results for trees on multiple cardinals , or with required or forbidden types of subtrees", "context_len": 32}}}, "cardinals": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 22, "context": ", and continued this work on exploring consistent possibilities for various types of trees , looking for results for trees on multiple cardinals , or with required or forbidden types of subtrees", "context_len": 32}}}, "elegance": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 81, "context": "`` Taxi '' ( November 1986 ) commented that being young and having no financial backing did not intimidate Davis from creating couture clothing of the highest level ; that respect should be paid to him and fashion magazine should acknowledge him and take the initiative to put him on the map ; and also that a lady dressed in Davis \u2019 s clothes would not only be taken seriously , but would be praised for her good taste and silent elegance - daring to detach herself from the uniforms of a working machine", "context_len": 94}}}, "partition": {"freq": 13, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 13, "word_index": 4, "context": "`` Todor\u010devi\u0107 obtained this partition relation in September 1984 , while lecturing on it in the Berkeley seminar , wrote up the notes of his lectures and circulated them in January 1985 and published the result later , in 1987", "context_len": 40}}}, "calculus": {"freq": 25, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 22, "word_index": 45, "context": "Also in the nineteenth century , Sim\u00e9on Denis Poisson described the definite integral as the difference of the antiderivatives [ F ( b ) F ( a ) ] at the endpoints a and b , describing what is now the first fundamental theorem of calculus", "context_len": 46}, "UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 5, "context": "The first fundamental theorem of calculus states that if the function f ( x ) is continuous , then", "context_len": 19}}}, "startling": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "As to the partition calculus in 1980 \u2019 s , `` Todor\u010devi\u0107 proved a startling square bracket partition result for the uncountable and introduced new technology whose ramifications are still unfolding , and proved a stepping up lemma for negative square bracket partition relations", "context_len": 44}}}, "bracket": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, 