book covers and endpapers in bookbinding and stationery", "context_len": 21}}}, "expense": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 14, "context": "It is a warning to the rich who would build their wealth at the expense of everyone else , as the poor will unite in arms to take their heads ( `` eat '' here not being used literally to mean cannibalism )", "context_len": 43}}}, "quadrennial": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "The 1984 AFC Asian Cup was the 8th edition of the men 's AFC Asian Cup , a quadrennial international football tournament organised by the Asian Football Confederation ( AFC )", "context_len": 31}}}, "bridgehead": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "In Operation Hush , marines were to land on the Belgian coast and there would be a breakout attack from Nieuwpoort and the Yser bridgehead", "context_len": 25}}}, "theropod": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 8, "context": "An example of this is the early Cretaceous theropod `` Caudipteryx zoui '' from northeastern China", "context_len": 16}}}, "ha": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 5, "context": "All together , about 89 ha of woodland is found within the town , making up 8 % of the town 's total land area", "context_len": 25}}}, "clepsydra": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 26, "context": "`` To define the length of a 'night watch ' at the summer solstice , one had to pour two mana of water into a cylindrical clepsydra ; its emptying indicated the end of the watch", "context_len": 36}}}, "johannes": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 0, "context": "Johannes Diderik van der Waals ( ; 23 November 1837 \u2013 8 March 1923 ) was a Dutch theoretical physicist and thermodynamicist", "context_len": 22}}}, "thermodynamicist": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "Johannes Diderik van der Waals ( ; 23 November 1837 \u2013 8 March 1923 ) was a Dutch theoretical physicist and thermodynamicist", "context_len": 22}}}, "pioneering": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 5, "context": "He became famous for his pioneering work on the equation of state for gases and liquids", "context_len": 16}, "UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 17, "context": "In 1953 it was renamed Sydney ( Kingsford Smith ) Airport after Charles Kingsford Smith , a pioneering Australian aviator", "context_len": 20}}}, "liquids": {"freq": 13, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 13, "word_index": 37, "context": "Diseases that can be infected through airborne transmission may be viruses , bacteria , or fungi , and they may be spread through breathing , talking , coughing , sneezing , raising of dust , spraying of liquids or even flushing toilets", "context_len": 42}}}, "condensation": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "His name is primarily associated with the Van der Waals equation of state that describes the behavior of gases and their condensation to the liquid phase", "context_len": 26}}}, "clusters": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 24, "context": "The leaves are evergreen and needle-like , 8\u201360 mm long , arranged in an open spiral on long shoots , and in dense spiral clusters of 15\u201345 together on short shoots ; they vary from bright grass-green to dark green to strongly glaucous pale blue-green , depending on the thickness of the white wax layer which protects the leaves from drying out", "context_len": 62}}}, "bound": {"freq": 26, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 17, "context": "On the other hand , treating all charges on the same footing ( disregarding whether they are bound or free charges ) , the generalized Amp\u00e8re 's equation ( also called the Maxwell\u2013Amp\u00e8re equation ) is ( see the `` proof '' section below ) :", "context_len": 46}, "NOUN": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 5, "context": "Treating free charges separately from bound charges , Amp\u00e8re 's equation including Maxwell 's correction in terms of the H-field is ( the H-field is used because it includes the magnetization currents , so JM does not appear explicitly , see H-field and also Note ) :", "context_len": 47}, "UNK": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 22, "context": "When a material is magnetized ( for example , by placing it in an external magnetic field ) , the electrons remain bound to their respective atoms , but behave as if they were orbiting the nucleus in a particular direction , creating a microscopic current", "context_len": 46}}}, "radii": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 39, "context": "His name is also associated with Van der Waals forces ( forces between stable molecules ) , with Van der Waals molecules ( small molecular clusters bound by Van der Waals forces ) , and with Van der Waals radii ( sizes of molecules )", "context_len": 45}}}, "foremost": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 24, "context": "As James Clerk Maxwell said , `` there can be no doubt that the name of Van der Waals will soon be among the foremost in molecular science", "context_len": 28}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "He was one of the foremost architects of his time and , apart from Wells , was engaged in work for the king at Windsor and at New College , Oxford University and Winchester Cathedral", "context_len": 35}}}, "intermolecular": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "In his 1873 thesis , Van der Waals noted that real gases were not ideal : He thought this was because there are intermolecular interactions", "context_len": 25}}}, "interactions": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 13, "context": "That molecular aspects such as size , shape , attraction , and multipolar interactions should form the basis for mathematical formulations of the thermodynamic and transport properties of fluids is presently considered an axiom", "context_len": 34}}}, "assumption": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 2, "context": "The key assumption behind the technique is that , in the long run , changes in molecular structure happen at a steady rate", "context_len": 23}}}, "spearheaded": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Spearheaded by Ernst Mach and Wilhelm Ostwald , a strong philosophical current that denied the existence of molecules arose towards the end of the 19th century", "context_len": 26}}}, "philosophical": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 7, "context": "He also played a cheerfully corrupt and philosophical private detective in the film noir `` Born to Kill '' ( 1947 ) and appeared as Squire Trelawney in `` Treasure Island '' ( 1972 )", "context_len": 35}}}, "unproven": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 4, "context": "Fermat 's theorem remained unproven until the work of 18th-century Swiss mathematician Leonhard Euler", "context_len": 14}}}, "fluids": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 18, "context": "At the time Van der Waals 's thesis was written ( 1873 ) , the molecular structure of fluids had not been accepted by most physicists , and liquid and vapor were often considered as chemically distinct", "context_len": 37}}}, "physicists": {"freq": 15, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 14, "word_index": 27, "context": "Since CEBAF has three complementary experiments running simultaneously , it was decided that the three data acquisition systems should be as similar as possible , so that physicists moving from one experiment to another would find a familiar environment", "context_len": 39}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "( Currently , physicists accept the fact that there are at least 11 dimensions in our universe : 1 time dimension and 10 spatial dimensions", "context_len": 25}}}, "vapor": {"freq": 13, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 30, "context": "At the time Van der Waals 's thesis was written ( 1873 ) , the molecular structure of fluids had not been accepted by most physicists , and liquid and vapor were often considered as chemically distinct", "context_len": 37}, "UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 15, "context": "During the following `` quiet '' period in October , the hydrothermal component of the vapor discharge steadily increased", "context_len": 19}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Refrigerants are chosen for the ease of converting them from liquid to vapor or vice versa , depending on their temperature and pressure", "context_len": 23}}}, "chemically": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 12, "context": "Organic foods are unique to the way other products are produced as chemically treated food can cause a lot of harm to the environment by decreasing the quality of soil and increasing energy use , carbon emissions , pesticides , and nitrate pollution", "context_len": 43}}}, "affirmed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "But Van der Waals 's work affirmed the reality of molecules and allowed an assessment of their size and attractive strength", "context_len": 21}}}, "revolutionized": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 3, "context": "The New Look revolutionized women 's dress and reestablished Paris as the center of the fashion world", "context_len": 17}}}, "characterizing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "By introducing parameters characterizing molecular size and attraction in constructing his equation of state , Van der Waals set the tone for modern molecular science", "context_len": 25}}}, "aspects": {"freq": 17, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 17, "word_index": 13, "context": "Nuclear energy policy is a national and international policy concerning some or all aspects of nuclear energy , such as mining for nuclear fuel , extraction and processing of nuclear fuel from the ore , electricity generation by nuclear power , enriching and storing spent nuclear fuel and nuclear fuel reprocessing", "context_len": 51}}}, "formulations": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 20, "context": "That molecular aspects such as size , shape , attraction , and multipolar interactions should form the basis for mathematical formulations of the thermodynamic and transport properties of fluids is presently considered an axiom", "context_len": 34}}}, "thermodynamic": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "That molecular aspects such as size , shape , attraction , and multipolar interactions should form the basis for mathematical formulations of the thermodynamic and transport properties of fluids is presently considered an axiom", "context_len": 34}, "UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 23, "context": "With the help of the Van der Waals 's equation of state , the critical-point parameters of gases could be accurately predicted from thermodynamic measurements made at much higher temperatures", "context_len": 30}}}, "measurements": {"freq": 15, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 15, "word_index": 4, "context": "In March 2005 , measurements by the Solar Wind Anisotropies ( SWAN ) instrument onboard the Solar and Heliospheric Observatory ( SOHO ) showed that the heliosphere , the solar wind-filled volume which prevents the solar system from becoming embedded in the local ( ambient ) interstellar medium , is not axisymmetrical , but is distorted , very likely under the effect of the local galactic magnetic field", "context_len": 68}}}, "nitrogen": {"freq": 46, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 35, "word_index": 22, "context": "He showed that , to grow , plants need ( as well as water and sunlight ) carbon dioxide , minerals and nitrogen compounds", "context_len": 24}, "UNK": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 8, "context": "In 1849 he discovered anhydrous nitric acid ( nitrogen pentoxide ) , a substance interesting as the first obtained of the 