": 28, "context": "Famous musicians who studied there include the trumpeter Alison Balsom , the composer Thomas Ad\u00e8s , the flautist Sir James Galway , the pianist Paul Lewis , the violinist Tasmin Little and the singers Kate Royal and Bryn Terfel", "context_len": 39}}}, "thumb": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 55, "context": "By convention , the direction of the vector area is given by the right hand grip rule ( curling the fingers of one 's right hand in the direction of the current around the loop , when the palm of the hand is `` touching '' the loop 's outer edge , and the straight thumb indicates the direction of the vector area and thus of the magnetic moment )", "context_len": 70}}}, "lutenists": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Weiss also taught other lutenists", "context_len": 5}}}, "forgot": {"freq": 9, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 9, "word_index": 6, "context": "Taoists thought that if someone `` forgot themselves '' , and let go of intentions , they would be able to `` move effortlessly '' ( wu wei , or `` non-action '' ) , and be in harmony with the Tao , like the animals , plants , and everything else", "context_len": 52}}}, "tablature": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "Not everyone can read Weiss ' music , because it was written in tablature notation", "context_len": 15}}}, "violin": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 25, "context": "She has a brother , opera singer actor Harry Danner , a sister , performer-turned-director Dorothy ( Dottie ) Danner , and a half-brother , violin maker William Moennig", "context_len": 29}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "She began violin lessons at a young age ; she later studied piano , flute , and guitar", "context_len": 18}}}, "instrumental": {"freq": 13, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 12, "word_index": 33, "context": "The week ending July 28 , 1958 was the final publication of the `` Most Played By Jockeys '' and `` Top 100 '' charts , both of which had Perez Prado 's instrumental version of `` Patricia '' ascending to the top", "context_len": 43}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Other Romantic composers often wrote short instrumental works which they called serenades", "context_len": 12}}}, "regina": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "His first opera , `` Zenobia , regina de Palmireni '' , was performed in Venice in 1694", "context_len": 18}}}, "concerto": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 34, "context": "Some of the arias are very difficult to sing , especially the long `` Martern aller Arten '' ( `` Tortures of all kinds '' ) sung by Konstanze , which is like a concerto movement", "context_len": 36}}}, "fugues": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "He was known by Johann Sebastian Bach , who wrote at least two fugues based on themes by Albinoni", "context_len": 19}}}, "sorry": {"freq": 14, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 13, "context": "Horrified , Evelina writes a letter to Lord Orville saying that she was sorry for what the Branghtons did , and the Branghtons had used her name without even telling her", "context_len": 31}, "UNK": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 12, "context": "That means that they do not believe anymore and that they are sorry for all the hurt it has caused", "context_len": 20}, "VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 7, "context": "Samuel made the people in Israel be sorry for their sins until he died", "context_len": 14}}}, "infinite": {"freq": 12, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 8, "context": "It has been conjectured that there are an infinite number of Wilson primes , and that the number of Wilson primes in an interval formula 3 is about", "context_len": 28}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "They are , however , not absolutely infinite", "context_len": 8}}}, "integers": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 17, "context": "In contrast to real numbers that vary `` smoothly '' , discrete mathematics studies objects such as integers , graphs , and statements in logic", "context_len": 25}}}, "composite": {"freq": 26, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 26, "word_index": 34, "context": "Basically , they proved that if a number is superabundant , the exponent of a larger prime number is never bigger than a smaller prime number during prime decomposition ( the process of a composite number become smaller prime numbers )", "context_len": 41}}}, "grouping": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 8, "context": "They are used a lot in geometry , grouping , and time measurement", "context_len": 13}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "The general shape of the island grouping looks like the body of a dragon with its head erect", "context_len": 18}}}, "arithmetic": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "They were ways of preparing for the quadrivium , which includes arithmetic , geometry , music and astronomy", "context_len": 18}}}, "gram": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 23, "context": "Ultimate ( often called Ultimate Frisbee in reference to the trademarked brand name ) is a non-contact team sport played with a 175 gram flying disc on a rectangular field", "context_len": 30}}}, "kilogram": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 23, "context": "`` This changes the meaning of `` gram '' to mean that the gram is 1000 times more than a gram : one kilogram is the same as 1000 grams", "context_len": 30}}}, "grams": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 29, "context": "`` This changes the meaning of `` gram '' to mean that the gram is 1000 times more than a gram : one kilogram is the same as 1000 grams", "context_len": 30}}}, "denominator": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 35, "context": "If its velocity reaches the speed of light ( which is `` c '' in this equation ) , formula 3 will equal one , and since that would leave one minus one in the denominator , there would be a divide by zero error", "context_len": 45}}}, "infinitely": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 25, "context": "In an attempt to share her experiences , she creates installations that immerse the viewer in her obsessive vision of endless dots and nets or infinitely mirrored space", "context_len": 28}}}, "irrational": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 0, "context": "Irrational numbers are numbers that can not be written as a fraction", "context_len": 12}}}, "transcendental": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 7, "context": "These are written as algebraic numbers or transcendental numbers", "context_len": 9}}}, "transfinite": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 0, "context": "Transfinite numbers are numbers that are `` infinite ''", "context_len": 9}}}, "absolutely": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 18, "context": "Even in 1908 , Camille Jullian wrote a comprehensive history of Gaul and took Caesar 's account as absolutely true", "context_len": 20}}}, "publishers": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 26, "context": "In response , Depp claimed that Heard was the one that had abused him before he went on , in 2018 , to unsuccessfully sue the publishers of the British tabloid `` The Sun '' for defamation in England for calling him a wifebeater", "context_len": 44}}}, "affiliation": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Affiliation", "context_len": 1}}}, "teletype": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Ken had brought a teletype terminal home one day in 1979 , and while looking through the host system 's catalog of programs , discovered the text adventure `` Colossal Cave Adventure ''", "context_len": 33}}}, "catalog": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 9, "context": "Often , a label deleted a single from its catalog after only one week , thus allowing the song to enter the Hot 100 , make a high debut and then decline in position as the one-time production of the retail single sold out", "context_len": 44}}}, "thrilled": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 13, "context": "He encouraged Roberta to join him in playing it , and she was thrilled by the game ; after Ken had brought an Apple II to their home , she played through other text adventures such as those by Scott Adams and Softape to study them", "context_len": 46}}}, "dissatisfied": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Dissatisfied with the text-only format , she realized that the graphics display capability of the Apple II could improve the adventure gaming experience", "context_len": 23}}}, "printout": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 40, "context": "With Ken 's help in some of the programming , Roberta designed `` Mystery House '' , inspired by the novel `` And Then There Were None '' and the board game `` Clue '' , using text commands and printout combined with graphics depicting the current setting", "context_len": 48}}}, "depicting": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 42, "context": "`` Leisem Jagoi `` ( ) ( literally , `` Dance of creation of the earth '' ) is a dance form enacted by imitating the movements of nine gods and seven goddesses creating the earth , followed by Laibou Jagoi , depicting the creation of human body and various activities of man , like weaving of clothes", "context_len": 58}}}, "modest": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 23, "context": "Yeo was less successful that the two bench bosses that preceded him ( Ron Mason and Rick Comley ) but did achieve a modest amount of success with the Lakers in his five seasons", "context_len": 34}}}, "static": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 7, "word_index":