ains respect on a business level", "context_len": 37}}}, "bagel": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 30, "context": "`` Taxi '' further observed that a customer from Henri Bendel would never suspect that the dress she just purchased was from a young designer who supported himself by making bagel sandwiches in a downtown coffee shop", "context_len": 37}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "He gave fashion commentary while he sort of made bagel sandwiches", "context_len": 11}}}, "flashy": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "`` Taxi '' ( November 1986 ) quoted Davis : Most people would rather spend money on flashy clothes that scream and spell expensive \u2019 , rather than purchasing understated elegant garments ''", "context_len": 33}}}, "scream": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 13, "context": "At 09:28:17 , eleven seconds into the descent , Cleveland heard a man scream into the cockpit radio : `` Mayday ! Mayday ! Mayday ! '' A second raspy shout went , `` Hey ! Get out of here ! '' Cleveland Air Traffic Controller John Werth did n't know the source of the call he heard , and could only make out what he heard as `` just some gruttural , gruttural sounds", "context_len": 75}}}, "spell": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 22, "context": "`` Taxi '' ( November 1986 ) quoted Davis : Most people would rather spend money on flashy clothes that scream and spell expensive \u2019 , rather than purchasing understated elegant garments ''", "context_len": 33}, "VERB": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 21, "context": "While mainland China uses only Hanyu Pinyin for almost all Chinese place names , Taiwan still uses Chinese postal romanization to spell their cities ' names , like Taipei , Taichung , and Kaohsiung", "context_len": 34}}}, "understated": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 29, "context": "`` Taxi '' ( November 1986 ) quoted Davis : Most people would rath