emist , a Chinese take away , a butchers , a post office and florist", "context_len": 22}}}, "unsure": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Historians are unsure why , but Hall 's life changed", "context_len": 10}}}, "bullock": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "On 14 April 1862 Gardiner and Hall robbed three bullock wagon drivers", "context_len": 12}}}, "tracker": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 30, "context": "On 1 March 1863 , Hall and bushrangers Patrick Daley ( Patsy ) and John O'Meally , were nearly captured in the Weddin mountains by Police Inspector Norton and black tracker Billy Dargin", "context_len": 33}}}, "trackers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Black trackers were aboriginals used by the police for their skills in following people in the bush", "context_len": 17}}}, "aboriginals": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Black trackers were aboriginals used by the police for their skills in following people in the bush", "context_len": 17}}}, "stagecoaches": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "In 1862 Cobb and Co had a stopping place for changing horses on their stagecoaches", "context_len": 15}}}, "ransom": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Instead he asked for a 500 ransom", "context_len": 7}}}, "gunfight": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 44, "context": "Two other men , James Gordon , alias James Mount ( known as `` The Old Man '' ) and John Dunleavy , joined the gang but Gordon was captured trying to flee in Victoria and Dunleavy surrendered after being badly wounded in a gunfight", "context_len": 45}}}, "powerless": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "The police seemed powerless to stop the Ben Hall gang", "context_len": 10}}}, "headstone": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN"