essionals as pseudoscience", "context_len": 15}}}, "contradict": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Philosopher and physicist Mario Bunge has written that telepathy would contradict laws of science and the claim that `` signals can be transmitted across space without fading with distance is inconsistent with physics ''", "context_len": 34}}}, "fading": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "Philosopher and physicist Mario Bunge has written that telepathy would contradict laws of science and the claim that `` signals can be transmitted across space without fading with distance is inconsistent with physics ''", "context_len": 34}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 34, "context": "In the 2004 German movie `` Der Untergang '' , Adolf Hitler is shown sitting in a dark room forlornly gazing at a painting of Frederick , possibly a reference to the dictator 's fading hopes for another Miracle of the House of Brandenburg", "context_len": 44}}}, "megabit": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "A megabit is a unit of information or computer storage that means one million bits , or one thousand kilobits", "context_len": 20}}}, "kilobits": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "2G phones transmit data at about the same speed as a 56kbit s ( kilobits per second ) dial-up modem would get", "context_len": 22}}}, "copywriter": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "Shigesato Itoi ( `` Itoi Shigesato '' , born November 10 , 1948 in Gumna ) is a famous Japanese copywriter , essayist , and game designer", "context_len": 27}}}, "disturbing": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 13, "context": "The movie was rated R by the MPAA for language , an intense disturbing situation , and brief drug use", "context_len": 20}}}, "cuvier": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "The tiger shark ( `` Galeocerdo cuvier '' ) is a species of requiem shark , and is the only member of the genus Galeocerdo", "context_len": 25}}}, "ovoviviparous": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 12, "context": "The tiger shark is the only species in its family which is ovoviviparous , giving birth to 10-82 pups at a time", "context_len": 22}}}, "sturdy": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "The front of the body is quite sturdy , but becomes more slim at the back", "context_len": 16}}}, "blunt": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 16, "context": "Smashers use this ability to attack snails , crabs , molluscs and rock oysters ; their blunt clubs enabling them to crack the shells of their prey into pieces", "context_len": 29}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "The beluga 's body is stout and has a small , blunt head with a small beak , tiny eyes and thick layers of blubber", "context_len": 25}}}, "recurved": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "The much smaller second dorsal fin is located at the front of the anal fin which is strongly recurved", "context_len": 19}}}, "jaws": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 1, "context": "The jaws of the tiger shark have large , sharp teeth which helps the shark to cut through the flesh and bones of their prey", "context_len": 25}}}, "fade": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "The black spots and stripes of the tiger shark are more visible on young ones , and they fade as the shark matures", "context_len": 23}}}, "murky": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "The tiger shark is found in many different kinds of marine habitats , but it usually prefers murky waters in coastal areas", "context_len": 22}}}, "estuaries": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 13, "context": "People worked to protect hundreds of miles of beache