kets in the upper jaw", "context_len": 9}}}, "echolocation": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 9, "context": "Like other toothed whales , the sperm whale uses echolocation , a way of sensing in which they emit high-pitched clicks and sense them as they bounce back off objects ( like prey )", "context_len": 34}}}, "sensing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "Like other toothed whales , the sperm whale uses echolocation , a way of sensing in which they emit high-pitched clicks and sense them as they bounce back off objects ( like prey )", "context_len": 34}}}, "emit": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 18, "context": "Like other toothed whales , the sperm whale uses echolocation , a way of sensing in which they emit high-pitched clicks and sense them as they bounce back off objects ( like prey )", "context_len": 34}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "Color vision is the capacity of an organism to distinguish objects based on the wavelengths ( or frequencies ) of the light they reflect , emit , or transmit", "context_len": 29}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Laser diodes emit less collimated light due to their short cavity , and therefore higher collimation requires a collimating lens", "context_len": 20}}}, "clicks": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "Like other toothed whales , the sperm whale uses echolocation , a way of sensing in which they emit high-pitched clicks and sense them as they bounce back off objects ( like prey )", "context_len": 34}}}, "bounce": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "Like other toothed whales , the sperm whale uses echolocation , a way of sensing in which they emit high-pitched clicks and sense them as they bounce back off objects ( like prey )", "context_len": 34}}}, "semitic": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Semitic languages are spoken by more than 470 million people across much of Western Asia , North Africa and the Horn of Africa , as well as in large communities of people from different countries in North America and Europe", "context_len": 40}}}, "wily": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 0, "context": "Wily , is a platform video game made by Capcom for the Nintendo Entertainment System game console", "context_len": 17}}}, "robots": {"freq": 15, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 15, "word_index": 18, "context": "Another difference is that the story behind each character is different in the cartoon for a lot of robots , like the Dinobots , Jetfire ( who is called Skyfire on TV ) , the Constructicons , and Omega Supreme", "context_len": 40}}}, "reprograms": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Wily , create humanoid robots ; Wily goes rogue and reprograms most of the robots for world domination", "context_len": 18}}}, "robot": {"freq": 9, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 10, "context": "In 2009 , he was cast as Bot , the robot superhero , on the children 's show `` Team Umizoomi '' through the relationships he had made at Nickelodeon on `` Blue 's Clues ''", "context_len": 36}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "We learn that the Transformers were once robot slaves who had to work for aliens called Quintessons", "context_len": 17}}}, "overcoming": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 15, "context": "From there you must find your way to the Robot Master , along the way overcoming many traps , pitfalls and other obstacles", "context_len": 23}}}, "pitfalls": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "From there you must find your way to the Robot Master , along the way overcoming many traps , pitfalls and other obstacles", "context_len": 23}}}, "scissors": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "laughter": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 12, "context": "Mood-setting music is sprinkled throughout the series , in lieu of audience laughter , in a way that resembles feature film more than other TV sitcoms", "context_len": 26}}}, "obeys": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "In the Bible , Saul loves and obeys God , until he stops listening to God and becomes greedy , losing God 's whole interest for him", "context_len": 27}}}, "grabs": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "When turning to leave , Saul grabs Samuel 's robe , and it tears", "context_len": 14}}}, "robe": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "When turning to leave , Saul grabs Samuel 's robe , and it tears", "context_len": 14}}}, "torments": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "Then the spirit of the Lord departs from Saul , and an evil spirit torments him", "context_len": 16}}}, "soothed": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 28, "context": "Saul takes David the shepherd , and the youngest son of Jesse , into his service to play a harp for him and so that he would be soothed when the evil spirit rests upon him", "context_len": 36}}}, "jealousy": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 2, "context": "Saul 's jealousy then began to heat into hatred , and he wanted to kill David , but not yet with his own hand - and so he asked David to marry his daughter , Merab , but David refused politely , and Merab was married to Adriel of Meholah", "context_len": 50}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "The reason for the murders has been identified as jealousy as Christine had dated the children 's stepfather on a holiday in 2006", "context_len": 23}}}, "fume": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "But Saul 's son Jonathan is bound to David in friendship , which makes his anger fume on Jonathan as well", "context_len": 21}}}, "leaning": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "In 2 Samuel , an Amalekite tells David he found Saul leaning on his spear after the battle and delivered the `` coup de gr\u00e2ce ''", "context_len": 26}}}, "anointed": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "David has the Amalekite put to death for accusing himself of killing the anointed king", "context_len": 15}, "VERB_Past": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 26, "context": "Many times David did not kill Saul when he had a chance to , but instead said , `` How can I kill the Lord 's anointed ? '' and spared Saul ; and many times Saul blessed David and repented , and determined to stop trying to kill David - but he always returned with a spear", "context_len": 58}}}, "decapitated": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 22, "context": "The victorious Philistines recover Saul 's body as well as those of his three sons who also died in the battle , decapitated them and displayed them on the wall of Beth-shan", "context_len": 32}}}, "retrieve": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 7, "context": "But at night the inhabitants of Jabesh-Gilead retrieve the bodies for cremation and burial ( )", "context_len": 16}}}, "cremation": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 13, "context": "The Hindu , Sikh , and Buddhist religions still use pyres for the cremation of dead people", "context_len": 17}}}, "buries": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Later on , David takes the bones of Saul and of his son Jonathan and buries them in Zela , in the tomb of his father ( )", "context_len": 28}}}, "ensued": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 33, "context": "However , after the death of King Saul , the tribe of Judah seceded from the rule of the House of Saul by proclaiming David as its king ( ) , and war ensued ( )", "cont