"POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Leave : A trio of carbons leave and become sugar", "context_len": 10}}}, "carbohydrate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "The carbohydrate products of the Calvin cycle are three-carbon sugar phosphate molecules , or 'glucose triose phosphates ' ( G3P )", "context_len": 21}}}, "phosphates": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "The carbohydrate products of the Calvin cycle are three-carbon sugar phosphate molecules , or 'glucose triose phosphates ' ( G3P )", "context_len": 21}}}, "fief": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 1, "context": "This fief was created in 911 by Charles the Simple King of France for Rollo , a leader of Northmen", "context_len": 20}}}, "meritorious": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "He served in the United States Army from 1969 to 1971 and earned the Army Commendation Medal for meritorious service", "context_len": 20}}}, "gen": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "Its front end is identical to the 10th gen Ford F-150", "context_len": 11}}}, "jellyfish": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 23, "context": "Ca2 ( calcium ) inside of different parts of cells like the mitochondria can make light when it reacts with a protein from jellyfish named aequorin", "context_len": 26}}}, "sting": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Humans can easily be killed by its sting", "context_len": 8}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "The investigations were conducted as undercover sting operations with the help of on-line watchdog group Perverted-Justice", "context_len": 16}}}, "rainfalls": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "December 2010 was the wettest on record , with 107 places getting their highest rainfalls ever", "context_len": 16}}}, "crocodiles": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 12, "context": "Examples of predators are hawks , eagles , falcons , cats , crocodiles , snakes , raptors , wolves , killer whales , lobsters , lions , and sharks", "context_len": 29}}}, "evacuees": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "1,200 people from Emerald were listed as evacuees", "context_len": 8}}}, "disruption": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Both towns were isolated for several days and there was major disruption to the drinking water supply and local agricultural production", "context_len": 21}}}, "transferring": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Blagojevich graduated from Chicago 's Foreman High School after transferring from Lane Technical High School", "context_len": 15}}}, "downstate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "Blagojevich finished strongly in Southern Illinois , winning 55 % of the primary vote downstate , enough to win a primary victory by a thin margin", "context_len": 26}}}, "outspending": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "In the general election , Blagojevich defeated Topinka and the Green Party 's Rich Whitney , outspending Topinka $ 27 million to $ 6 million", "context_len": 25}}}, "pardoning": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 30, "context": "On May 31 , 2018 , President Donald Trump , soon after having pardoned commentator Dinesh D'Souza , told reporters that he was considering reducing Blagojevich 's sentence ( without pardoning him )", "context_len": 33}}}, "enriching": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 41, "context": "Nuclear energy policy is a national and international policy concerning some or all aspects of nuclear energy , such as mining for nuclear fuel , extraction and processing of nuclear fuel from the ore , electricity generation by nuclear power , enriching and storing spent nuclear fuel and nuclear fuel reprocessing", "context_len": 51}}}, "marsupial": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "The Daintree Rainforest contains 30 % of the frog , marsupial and reptile species in Australia , and 65 % of Australia 's bat and butterfly species", "context_len": 27}}}, "minimize": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 24, "context": "So , the surface will push back against any curvature in much the same way as a ball pushed uphill will push back to minimize its gravitational potential energy", "context_len": 29}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "The minimize , maximize and close window buttons are based on Windows Vista", "context_len": 13}}}, "cassowary": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "The Daintree Region is home to a number of rare and endangered species , including the southern cassowary and Bennett 's tree-kangaroo", "context_len": 22}}}, "astonishing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "It is listed as an important bird area , but might just as well be listed for its fungi , which are said to be astonishing", "context_len": 26}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Because Renesmee is growing at an astonishing rate , she looks older than her calendar age", "context_len": 16}}}, "saltwater": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 5, "context": "They are usually found in saltwater as they can not survive in freshwater", "context_len": 13}}}, "musky": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Animals include the saltwater crocodile and the musky rat-kangaroo", "context_len": 9}}}, "supercontinent": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 21, "context": "Fossils of the giant `` Beelzebufo '' from Cretaceous Madagascar suggest that the subfamily may have once ranged throughout the prehistoric supercontinent of Gondwana", "context_len": 24}}}, "clinker": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "The landmark building got its name from the red clinker bricks with which it is covered", "context_len": 16}}}, "modelled": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 32, "context": "In the US , the Walt Disney World resort recreated a Kenyan village in the Africa section of the Disney 's Animal Kingdom theme park named `` Harambe '' , which is modelled after Mombasa", "context_len": 35}}}, "reunified": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "After German reunification , the administration of reunified Berlin officially moved into the Rotes Rathaus on 1 October 1991", "context_len": 19}}}, "linden": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 19, "context": "In the course of the building of the Nord-S\u00fcd-Tunnel for the Berlin S-Bahn in 1934 35 most of the linden trees were cut down and during the last days of World War II the remaining trees were destroyed or cut down for firewood", "context_len": 43}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "It was replaced by a boulevard of linden trees planted in 1647 , stretching from the city palace to the gates of the city , by order of the Great Elector Frederick William", "context_len": 33}}}, "lime": {"freq": 18, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 11, "context": "The same surface tension demonstration can be done with water , lime water or even saline , but only if the liquid does not adhere to the flat surface material", "context_len": 30}, "NOUN": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 40, "context": "`` Burning '' ( calcination ) converts them into the highly caustic material `` quicklime '' ( calcium oxide ) , and , through the addition of water , into the less caustic , but still strongly alkaline `` slaked lime '' ( calcium hydroxide )", "context_len": 46}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Key lime pie", "context_len": 3}}}, "grassed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "It is named for its linden ( lime in British English ) trees that line the grassed pedestrian mall in the middle of the road", "context_len": 25}}}, "bridle": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 15, "context": "Unter den Linden at the heart of the historic section of Berlin developed from a bridle path laid out by Elector John George of Brandenburg in the 16th century to reach his hunting grounds in the Tiergarten", "context_len": 37}}}, "grandest": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "By the 19th century , as Berlin grew and expanded to the west , Unter den Linden became the best-known and grandest street in Berlin", "context_len": 25}}}, "replanted": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "The present-day linden were replanted in the 1950s , they are affected by air pollution as well as by soil contamination", "context_len": 21}}}, "prewar": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 30, "context": "The Prussian Mint Edict of May 1763 revalued the national currency , stabilizing the rates of highly depreciated coinage and mandating that the payments of taxes be in currency of prewar value", "context_len": 32}}}, "adorn": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "Well-known statues of Alexander and Wilhelm von Humboldt in front of the university as well as of the Prussian generals Scharnhorst and B\u00fclow also adorn the street", "context_len": 27}}}, "maquiladoras": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "The predominant activity is industry , including domestic heavy , light industries , consumer goods production , and to a smaller extent `` maquiladoras ''", "context_len": 25}}}, "pathway": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "A bridle path is a pathway or trail between two places", "context_len": 11}}}, "celibate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Many historians consider him to be bisexual and perhaps possibly celibate in his later life", "context_len": 15}}}, "bureaucracy": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 18, "context": "Frederick also presided over other important modernization efforts in Prussia , including the establishment of a modern governmental bureaucracy , the cultivation of one of Europe 's most highly-regarded educational systems , and the abolition torture and corporal punishment", "context_len": 39}}}, "patronized": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Frederick patronized the arts and philosophers , and wrote flute music", "context_len": 11}}}, "arrange": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 8, "context": "In 1732 , Queen Sophia Dorothea tried to arrange a dual marriage of Frederick and his sister Wilhelmina with Amelia and Frederick , the children of her brother , King George II of Great Britain", "context_len": 35}}}, "bribed": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 20, "context": "Fearing an alliance between Prussia and Great Britain , Field Marshal von Seckendorff , the Austrian ambassador in Berlin , bribed Field Marshal von Grumbkow , the Prussian Minister of War , and Benjamin Reichenbach , Prussian ambassador in London", "context_len": 40}}}, "discreetly": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "They pair discreetly slandered the British and Prussian courts in the eyes of the two kings", "context_len": 16}}}, "slandered": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "They pair discreetly slandered the British and Prussian courts in the eyes of the two kings", "context_len": 16}}}, "statecraft": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "Instead of returning to Berlin , however , he was forced to stay in K\u00fcstrin and began learning statecraft and administration for the War and Estates Departments on 20 November", "context_len": 30}}}, "eased": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Tensions eased slightly when Frederick William visited K\u00fcstrin a year later , and Frederick was allowed to visit Berlin on the occasion of his sister Wilhelmina 's marriage to Margrave Frederick of Bayreuth on 20 November 1731", "context_len": 37}}}, "renouncing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Frederick himself proposed marrying Maria Theresa of Austria in return for renouncing the succession", "context_len": 14}}}, "plagued": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 22, "context": "He had little in common with his bride and resented the political marriage as an example of the Austrian interference which had plagued Prussia since 1701", "context_len": 26}}}, "apartments": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 26, "context": "Once Frederick secured the throne in 1740 , he would not let Elisabeth visit his court in Potsdam , and instead gave her Sch\u00f6nhausen Palace and apartments at the Berliner Stadtschloss", "context_len": 31}}}, "happiest": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "He spent his time reading , watching dramatic plays , making and listening to music , and regarded this time as one of the happiest of his life", "context_len": 28}}}, "guideline": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "The works of Niccol\u00f2 Machiavelli , such as `` The Prince '' , were considered a guideline for the behaviour of a king in Frederick 's age", "context_len": 27}}}, "modernize": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Frederick 's goal was to modernize and unite his vulnerably disconnected lands ; toward this end , he fought wars mainly against Austria , whose Habsburg dynasty reigned as Holy Roman Emperors , almost continuously from the 15th century until 1806", "context_len": 41}}}, "vulnerably": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Frederick 's goal was to modernize and unite his vulnerably disconnected lands ; toward this end , he fought wars mainly against Austria , whose Habsburg dynasty reigned as Holy Roman Emperors , almost continuously from the 15th century until 1806", "context_len": 41}}}, "frugal": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "Frederick established Prussia as the fifth and smallest European great power by using the resources his frugal father had cultivated", "context_len": 20}}}, "prussian": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Prussian possession of Silesia gave the kingdom control over the Oder River", "context_len": 12}}}, "swiftly": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "It displays remarkable excavation abilities , swiftly hiding itself from predators like foxes and owls by completely burying itself in a matter of seconds", "context_len": 24}}}, "forcible": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "He faced widespread criticism for his attack on neutral Saxony and for his forcible incorporation of the Saxon forces into the Prussian army following the Siege of Pirna in October 1756", "context_len": 31}}}, "geniuses": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Frederick is often admired as one of the greatest tactical geniuses of all time , especially for his usage of the oblique order of battle", "context_len": 25}}}, "oblique": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "Frederick is often admired as one of the greatest tactical geniuses of all time , especially for his usage of the oblique order of battle", "context_len": 25}}}, "numerically": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "Even more important were his operational successes , especially preventing the unification of numerically superior opposing armies and being at the right place at the right time to keep enemy armies out of Prussian core territory", "context_len": 36}}}, "backwater": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Frederick transformed Prussia from a European backwater into an economically strong and politically reformed state", "context_len": 15}}}, "modernizing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "The modernizing mechanisms and technology of the state also enabled Frederick , in 1747 , to undertake a massive six-year drainage and `` reclamation '' program in the country 's northern marsh-land", "context_len": 32}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "They continued modernizing Japan during the Meiji Restoration", "context_len": 8}}}, "reclamation": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 20, "context": "This platform included removal of national banks , low interest government loans , free and limitless coinage of silver , reclamation of excess railroad lands taken by the government , a graduated income tax , and direct election of United States senators", "context_len": 42}}}, "taming": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "This rationalist-mided program , which Frederick saw as the `` taming '' and `` conquering '' of `` useless '' and `` barbarous '' nature , created roughly 150,000 acres of arable farmland , but also eliminated vast swaths of natural habitat , destroyed the region 's biodiversity , and displaced numerous indigenous communities", "context_len": 54}}}, "barbarous": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 22, "context": "This rationalist-mided program , which Frederick saw as the `` taming '' and `` conquering '' of `` useless '' and `` barbarous '' nature , created roughly 150,000 acres of arable farmland , but also eliminated vast swaths of natural habitat , destroyed the region 's biodiversity , and displaced numerous indigenous communities", "context_len": 54}}}, "swaths": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 38, "context": "This rationalist-mided program , which Frederick saw as the `` taming '' and `` conquering '' of `` useless '' and `` barbarous '' nature , created roughly 150,000 acres of arable farmland , but also eliminated vast swaths of natural habitat , destroyed the region 's biodiversity , and displaced numerous indigenous communities", "context_len": 54}}}, "lucrative": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 25, "context": "With the help of French experts , Frederick also reorganized Prussia 's taxation policy , implementing a system of indirect taxation , which was more lucrative than the previous policy of direct taxation", "context_len": 33}}}, "eminent": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Frederick also commissioned the eminent Prussian merchant Johann Ernst Gotzkowsky to help promote trade", "context_len": 14}}}, "levies": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Gotzkowsky directed Frederick to reform the Prussian system of toll levies and import restrictions , and to construct a major a silk factory in an effort to compete with the French silk trade", "context_len": 33}}}, "depreciating": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "The effects of the Seven Years ' War and the acquisition of Silesia had transformed the economy , depreciating the national currency and leading to high nation-wide inflation", "context_len": 28}}}, "revalued": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "The Prussian Mint Edict of May 1763 revalued the national currency , stabilizing the rates of highly depreciated coinage and mandating that the payments of taxes be in currency of prewar value", "context_len": 32}}}, "stabilizing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "The Prussian Mint Edict of May 1763 revalued the national currency , stabilizing the rates of highly depreciated coinage and mandating that the payments of taxes be in currency of prewar value", "context_len": 32}}}, "depreciated": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "The Prussian Mint Edict of May 1763 revalued the national currency , stabilizing the rates of highly depreciated coinage and mandating that the payments of taxes be in currency of prewar value", "context_len": 32}}}, "mandating": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "The Prussian Mint Edict of May 1763 revalued the national currency , stabilizing the rates of highly depreciated coinage and mandating that the payments of taxes be in currency of prewar value", "context_len": 32}}}, "undertook": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Other European rulers soon undertook similar monetary reforms , which helped to lower region-wide prices", "context_len": 15}}}, "underscoring": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 52, "context": "After the acquisition of Royal Prussia ( West Prussia ) in 1772 , Frederick also changed his title from the `` King `` in '' Prussia , '' which had been the royal title used since the coronation of Frederick I , to the `` King `` of '' Prussia , '' underscoring the increasing prominence of his state and his own importance as a ruler", "context_len": 66}}}, "unprejudiced": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "As an example of this practical-minded but not fully unprejudiced tolerance , Frederick wrote in his `` Testament politique '' that :", "context_len": 22}}}, "integrating": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 21, "context": "It follows that given a surface , we do not need to stick to any unique parametrization ; but , when integrating vector fields , we do need to decide in advance which direction the normal will point to , and then choose any parametrization consistent with that direction", "context_len": 49}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 30, "context": "Just as a line integral allows one to integrate over an arbitrary curve ( of one dimension ) , a surface integral can be thought of as a double integral integrating over a two-dimensional surface", "context_len": 35}}}, "financing": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 30, "context": "Since the civil rights movement of the 1950s and 1960s , and especially since the Civil Rights Act of 1968 prohibited racial discrimination concerning the sale , rental , and financing of housing , the number of sundown towns has decreased", "context_len": 41}}}, "rococo": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 29, "context": "However , the king preferred spending his time in his summer residence Potsdam , where he built the palace of Sanssouci , the most important work of Northern German rococo", "context_len": 30}}}, "carefree": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 8, "context": "Sanssouci , which translates from French as `` carefree '' or `` without worry '' , was a refuge for Frederick", "context_len": 21}}}, "preferring": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 34, "context": "The people of Berlin always cheered the king when he returned to the city from provincial tours or military reviews , but Frederick took no pleasure from his popularity with the common folk , preferring instead the company of his pet Italian greyhounds , whom he referred to as his 'marquises de Pompadour ' as a jibe at Madame de Pompadour", "context_len": 61}}}, "greyhounds": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 42, "context": "The people of Berlin always cheered the king when he returned to the city from provincial tours or military reviews , but Frederick took no pleasure from his