it on the radius of the rotating disk , he will measure the radius to be the same as he would measure it to be if the disk were stationary , since the radius is not affected by the Lorentz contraction ( the radius is perpendicular to the direction of motion )", "context_len": 60}}}, "stationary": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 37, "context": "If an observer `` Y '' were to sit on the radius of the rotating disk , he will measure the radius to be the same as he would measure it to be if the disk were stationary , since the radius is not affected by the Lorentz contraction ( the radius is perpendicular to the direction of motion )", "context_len": 60}}}, "curvature": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 14, "context": "Physicists began to realize that the accelerated angular motion of the disk caused a curvature in spacetime , therefore distorting the normal flat geometric plane , causing the circumference to be greater than 2 r", "context_len": 35}}}, "distorting": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "Physicists began to realize that the accelerated angular motion of the disk caused a curvature in spacetime , therefore distorting the normal flat geometric plane , causing the circumference to be greater than 2 r", "context_len": 35}}}, "ingenious": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Using an ingenious argument concerning the equivalence principle , Albert Einstein showed that the curvature in spacetime caused by the rotated disk could be a logical explanation for gravity", "context_len": 29}}}, "freeze": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 20, "context": "Beginning in the 1980s , many anti-nuclear power activists began shifting their interest , by joining a rapidly growing nuclear freeze movement , and the primary concern about nuclear hazards in the USA changed from the problems of nuclear power plants to the prospects of nuclear war", "c