elf further :", "context_len": 7}}}, "guyed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "This list has guyed masts , towers , skyscrapers and chimneys", "context_len": 11}}}, "skyscrapers": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 5, "context": "Brisbane has more than 50 skyscrapers more than 100 metres tall , the third most of any city in Oceania ( after Sydney and Melbourne )", "context_len": 26}}}, "chimneys": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "Observation towers , radio masts , chimneys and other structures are not included", "context_len": 13}}}, "spires": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 0, "context": "Spires on top of buildings count onto its height , but antennas do not", "context_len": 14}}}, "subcommittees": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 31, "context": "The other group that chooses people to add to the Hall of Fame is called the Veterans Committee , which since 2011 has been split into three separate groups ( or subcommittees )", "context_len": 33}}}, "umpires": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 33, "context": "The Veterans Committee votes on people who are not eligible for the BBWAA ballot players who have been retired for 20 or more years , managers , team and league executives , and umpires", "context_len": 34}}}, "innovators": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "He has been called one of the most important innovators of funk music , next to James Brown and Sly Stone", "context_len": 21}}}, "florist": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "There are also two shops , a chemist , a Chinese take away , a butchers , a post office and florist", "context_len": 22}}}, "growling": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "Melodic death metal bands may use normal singing some times , where death metal bands nearly always use growling", "context_len": 19}}}, "falsettos": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "He has also been noted for his falsettos", "context_len": 8}}}, "nu": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 9, "context": "In the mid-2000s , they changed their style from nu metal to emo and alternative rock", "context_len": 16}}}, "powering": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 22, "context": "The 152-turbine project by Scottish and Southern Energy , which was approved by the Scottish Parliament in July 2008 , capable of powering 320,000 homes , and will be larger than the 322 MW Whitelee Wind Farm near Glasgow", "context_len": 39}}}, "nominal": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "It will consist of an individual wind farm with 300 individual wind turbines with a nominal output of around 2 MW which will deliver up to 600 MW of power , enough to power over 393,000 homes , with a capital investment required of approximately US $ 750 million", "context_len": 49}}}, "motorbike": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "His prized possession during childhood was his flying motorbike", "context_len": 9}}}, "evade": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "Harry found out , after a year of believing otherwise , that Sirius was an innocent man , and helped him evade capture from the Ministry of Magic", "context_len": 28}}}, "resurrected": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 17, "context": "He returned during Harry 's 7th year along with James , Lily and Remus , after being resurrected with the help of the Resurrection stone in a hazy form", "context_len": 29}}}, "hazy": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "He returned during Harry 's 7th year along with James , Lily and Remus , after being resurrected with the help of the Resurrection stone in a hazy form", "context_len": 29}}}, "godson": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 7, "context": "He \u2019 s even related to his godson , Harry Potter , through Dorea Potter ( n\u00e9e Black ) who is a distant relative to Harry and James Potter", "context_len": 29}}}, "jukebox": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 25, "context": "`` Billboard '' eventually created a fourth singles popularity chart that combined all aspects of a single \u2019 s performance ( sales , airplay and jukebox activity ) , based on a point system that typically gave sales ( purchases ) more weight than radio airplay", "context_len": 46}}}, "jukeboxes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "ascending": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 39, "context": "The week ending July 28 , 1958 was the final publication of the `` Most Played By Jockeys '' and `` Top 100 '' charts , both of which had Perez Prado 's instrumental version of `` Patricia '' ascending to the top", "context_len": 43}}}, "methodology": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 24, "context": "During the first forty years of the rock era , no song had ever debuted at number one ; since a 1995 change in methodology , nineteen songs have", "context_len": 29}}}, "concurrent": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 12, "context": "Fred Muggs , did n't hurt his genial manner , but his concurrent seriousness in dealing with news stories and ability to clearly explain abstract concepts earned him the nickname `` The Communicator '' and eventually won praise from critics and viewers alike", "context_len": 43}}}, "moot": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "This started to become a moot point by 1972 , as most major record labels solidified a trend they had started in the 1960s by putting the same song on both sides of the singles it serviced to radio", "context_len": 39}}}, "solidified": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "This started to become a moot point by 1972 , as most major record labels solidified a trend they had started in the 1960s by putting the same song on both sides of the singles it serviced to radio", "context_len": 39}}}, "overtake": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "Further problems arose when , in several cases , a B-side would eventually overtake the A-side in popularity , thus prompting record labels to release a new single , featuring the former B-side as the A-side , along with a `` new '' B-side", "context_len": 44}}}, "longstanding": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "A longstanding policy of the Hot 100 chart was that songs must be sold as a single", "context_len": 17}}}, "phased": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 18, "context": "However , during the 1990s major record labels claimed that singles reduced album sales , so they were phased out", "context_len": 20}}}, "insiders": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "In response to debate , conflicts and requests by the music artists and insiders , `` Billboard '' included airplay-only singles ( or `` album cuts '' ) in the Hot 100", "context_len": 32}}}, "overhaul": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "This is the first major overhaul of the Hot 100 's chart formula since December 1998", "context_len": 16}}}, "shaken": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 49, "context": "Ten years after the incident , Damon Hill , who drove for the Williams-Renault team at the time , described the feeling after the crash : `` We all brushed ourselves off and carried on qualifying , reassured that our cars were tough as tanks and we could be shaken but not hurt", "context_len": 53}}}, "factored": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "were all combined and factored into the song \u2019 s performance on the Hot 100 , as the structure , lyrics and melody were the same", "context_len": 26}}}, "scenario": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "The first such example of this scenario is Jennifer Lopez \u2019 `` I 'm Real ''", "context_len": 16}}}, "midst": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "Originally entering the Hot 100 in its album version , a `` remix '' was issued in the midst of its chart run that featured rapper Ja Rule", "context_len": 28}}}, "resurgence": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Exceptions are made to re-releases and sudden resurgence in popularity of tracks that have taken a very long time to gain mainstream success", "context_len": 23}}}, "cumulative": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 32, "context": "Songs at the peak of their popularity at the time of the November December chart-year cutoff many times end up ranked on the following year 's chart as well , as their cumulative points are split between the two chart-years , but often are ranked lower than they would have been had the peak occurred in a single year", "context_len": 59}}}, "yearlong": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "After `` Billboard '' began obtaining sales and airplay information from Nielsen SoundScan , the year-end charts are now calculated by a very straightforward cumulative total of yearlong sales and airplay points", "context_len": 32}}}, "hypothetically": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "This gives a more accurate picture of any given year \u2019 s most popular tracks , as a song that hypothetically spent nine weeks at number one in March could possibly have earned fewer cumulative points than a song that spent six weeks at number three in January", "context_len": 48}}}, "cutoff": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Songs at the peak of their popularity at the time of the November December chart-year cutoff many times end up ranked on the following year 's chart as well , as their cumulative points are split between the two chart-years , but often are ranked lower than they would have been had the peak occurred in a single year", "context_len": 59}}}, "gauge": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 13, "context": "Few music historians believe that the Hot 100 has been a perfectly accurate gauge of the most popular songs for each week or year", "context_len": 24}}}, "payola": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "For example , during the 1950s and 1960s , payola and other problems skewed the numbers in largely undetectable ways", "context_len": 20}}}, "skewed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "For example , during the 1950s and 1960s , payola and other problems skewed the numbers in largely undetectable ways", "context_len": 20}}}, "undetectable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "For example , during the 1950s and 1960s , payola and other problems skewed the numbers in largely undetectable ways", "context_len": 20}}}, "discounting": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 29, "context": "Numerous artists have taken deliberate steps to maximize their chart positions by such tactics as timing a single 's debut to face the weakest possible competition , or massively discounting the price of singles to the point where each individual sale represented a financial loss", "context_len": 45}}}, "withhold": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Meanwhile , other artists would deliberately withhold even their most marketable songs in order to boost album sales", "context_len": 18}}}, "marketable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Meanwhile , other artists would deliberately withhold even their most marketable songs in order to boost album sales", "context_len": 18}}}, "unavailable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "Particularly in the 1990s , many of the most heavily played MTV and radio hits were unavailable for separate purchase", "context_len": 20}}}, "countervailing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Because of such countervailing strategies , it can not be said that a Hot 100 chart necessarily lists the country 's 100 most popular or successful songs", "context_len": 27}}}, "overemphasis": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Some critics have argued that an overemphasis on a limited number of singles has distorted record industry development efforts , and there are nearly as many critics of the Hot 100 as there are supporters", "context_len": 35}}}, "splintering": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "The ongoing splintering of Top 40 radio in the early 1990s led stations to lean into specific formats , meaning that practically no station would play the wide array of genres that typically composed each weekly Hot 100 chart", "context_len": 39}}}, "lean": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "The ongoing splintering of Top 40 radio in the early 1990s led stations to lean into specific formats , meaning that practically no station would play the wide array of genres that typically composed each weekly Hot 100 chart", "context_len": 39}}}, "utilizing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 19, "context": "In materials science , physics , chemistry , and molecular biology , a beamline leads to the experimental endstation utilizing particle beams from a particle accelerator , synchrotron light obtained from a synchrotron , or neutrons from a spallation source or research reactor", "context_len": 43}}}, "fm": {"freq": 2, "P