 of a bottle of Worcestershire sauce from England sold under the name `` The Original & amp ; Genuine Lea & amp ; Perrins Worcestershire Sauce '' by Lea & amp ; Perrins , Limited , lists the following ingredients : malt vinegar ( from barley ) , spirit vinegar , molasses , sugar , salt , anchovies , tamarind extract , onions , garlic , spice and flavouring", "context_len": 71}}}, "cloves": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 35, "context": ", lists these ingredients on the bottle made in the United States : vinegar , molasses , high fructose corn syrup , anchovies , water , onions , salt , garlic , tamarind concentrate , cloves , natural flavorings and chili pepper extract", "context_len": 43}}}, "gradients": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Fluxbox can show some eye candy such as : colors , gradients , borders , and several other basic appearance settings can be changed", "context_len": 24}}}, "enhancements": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Enhancements can also be provided by using iDesk or fbdesk , or the ROX Desktop", "context_len": 15}}}, "tabbed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Fluxbox also has several features Blackbox does not have , including tabbed windows and a configurable titlebar", "context_len": 17}}}, "linux": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "It is currently the default window manager of antiX , a linux distribution based on MEPIS and designed for old computers , PCFluxboxOS , a remaster of PCLinuxOS , and LinguasOS , a Live CD distribution for professional translators", "context_len": 39}}}, "remaster": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "It is currently the default window manager of antiX , a linux distribution based on MEPIS and designed for old computers , PCFluxboxOS , a remaster of PCLinuxOS , and LinguasOS , a Live CD distribution for professional translators", "context_len": 39}}}, "remastering": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "DSL was originally based on Model-K , a 22 MB stripped-down version of Knoppix , but soon after was based on Knoppix proper , allowing much easier remastering and improvements", "context_len": 30}}}, "plugins": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "As of June 2008 , the MyDSL servers were hosting over 900 applications , plugins , and other extensions", "context_len": 19}}}, "advertised": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "The `` testing '' area is for newly submitted extensions that theoretically work 'as advertised ' , but may have any number of bugs", "context_len": 24}}}, "bugs": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 23, "context": "The `` testing '' area is for newly submitted extensions that theoretically work 'as advertised ' , but may have any number of bugs", "context_len": 24}}}, "considerations": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "Strategic considerations", "context_len": 2}}}, "seaplane": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 17, "context": "The Imperial Japanese Navy ( IJN ) had occupied Tulagi in May 1942 and had constructed a seaplane base nearby", "context_len": 20}}}, "airfield": {"freq": 38, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 35, "word_index": 40, "context": "Following approval of an environmental impact statement filed in August 1973 , the base was designated an Armed Forces Reserve Center for which the Navy was designated host , and the California Army National Guard was charged with operating the airfield", "context_len": 41}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "The Japanese naval construction staff and combat troops had abandoned the airfield area and fled about west to the Matanikau River and Point Cruz area", "context_len": 25}, "VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 26, "context": "In 1940 , in World War II , the site was taken over by the Australian government and a Royal Australian Air Force ( RAAF ) airfield known as Empire Air Training Scheme No 1 Wireless Air Gunners School was begun ( EATS 1 WAGS ) at the Ballarat Showgrounds on 22 April 1940", "context_len": 54}}}, "marshall": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Marshall was against King 's proposed attacks and asked who would command the operation", "context_len": 14}}}, "turner": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Turner", "context_len": 1}}}, "planners": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 9, "context": "To get them into battle quickly , the operation planners had reduced their supplies to only 60 days", "context_len": 18}}}, "seaplanes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "carrier aircraft bombed Japanese forces on the target islands and destroyed 15 Japanese seaplanes at their base near Tulagi", "context_len": 19}}}, "afire": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 32, "context": "During the landing operations on 7 and 8 August , Japanese naval aircraft based at Rabaul , under the command of Sadayoshi Yamada , attacked the Allied forces several times , setting afire the transport USS `` George F", "context_len": 39}}}, "elliot": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Elliot '' ( which sank two days later ) and heavily damaging the destroyer", "context_len": 14}}}, "unloaded": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 37, "context": "As a result of the loss of carrier-based air cover , Turner pulled back his ships from Guadalcanal , even though less than half of the supplies and heavy equipment needed by the troops ashore had been unloaded", "context_len": 38}, "VERB_Past": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 6, "context": "That night , as the transports unloaded , two groups of Allied cruisers and destroyers , under the command of British Rear Admiral Victor Crutchley VC , were defeated by a Japanese force of seven cruisers and one destroyer from the 8th Fleet based at Rabaul and Kavieng and commanded by Japanese Vice Admiral Gunichi Mikawa", "context_len": 56}}}, "destroyers": {"freq": 43, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 43, "word_index": 14, "context": "That night , as the transports unloaded , two groups of Allied cruisers and destroyers , under the command of British Rear Admiral Victor Crutchley VC , were defeated by a Japanese force of seven cruisers and one destroyer from the 8th Fleet based at Rabaul and Kavieng and commanded by Japanese Vice Admiral Gunichi Mikawa", "context_len": 56}}}, "dysentery": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Allied troops got sick with dysentery soon after the landings , with one in five Marines sick by mid-August", "context_len": 19}}}, "coconuts": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "Although some of the Korean construction workers surrendered to the Marines , most of the Japanese and Korean gathered to the west and ate coconuts", "context_len": 25}}}, "perimeter": {"freq": 17, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 17, "word_index": 12, "context": "At the same time that Hyakutake 's troops were attacking the Lunga perimeter , Japanese aircraft carriers and other large warships led by Isoroku Yamamoto moved near the southern Solomon Islands", "context_len": 31}}}, "platoon": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 14, "context": "In the United States Army , for example , a second lieutenant leads a platoon made up of two or more squads or about 16 to 44 soldiers", "context_len": 28}}}, "fleets": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 22, "context": "On 24 and 25 August , the two carrier forces fought the Battle of the Eastern Solomons , which resulted in both fleets pulling back from the area after taking some damage", "context_len": 32}}}, "downed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "More than half of the downed U", "context_len": 7}}}, "aircrews": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 14, "context": "Nor could they replace their highly trained and veteran crews , especially the naval aircrews , nearly as quickly as the Allies", "context_len": 22}}}, "convoys": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 15, "context": "A separate attempt to establish bases in the central Solomons to use to send barge convoys to Guadalcanal also failed because of Allied air attacks", "context_len": 25}}}, "technicians": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "They provided the Marines at Lunga with more food , ammunition , aircraft fuel , and aircraft technicians", "context_len": 18}}}, "brigade": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 10, "context": "A barge convoy took another 1,000 soldiers of Kawaguchi 's brigade , under the command of Colonel Akinosuke Oka , to Kamimbo , west of the Lunga perimeter", "context_len": 28}}}, "depot": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "In Tasimboko , Edson 's troops discovered Kawaguchi 's main supply depot , including large stockpiles of food , ammunition , medical supplies , and a powerful shortwave radio", "context_len": 29}}}, "stockpiles": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "In Tasimboko , Edson 's troops discovered Kawaguchi 's main supply depot , including large stockpiles of food , ammunition , medical supplies , and a powerful shortwave radio", "context_len": 29}}}, "undefended": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "The ridge , called Lunga Ridge , had a good approach to the airfield and it was undefended", "context_len": 18}}}, "staffs": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "In an emergency meeting , the top Japanese IJA and IJN command staffs decided that , Guadalcanal might develop into the most important battle of the war", "context_len": 27}}}, "recapture": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 10, "context": "Hyakutake sent more troops to Guadalcanal for another attempt to recapture Henderson Field", "context_len": 13}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "At the end of `` Closing Time '' , on the day she receives her doctorate , the Silence and Kovarian recapture River", "context_len": 23}}}, "reinforcement": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 12, "context": "The herding dog breed has had over a hundred years of genetic reinforcement ( to strengthen ) to provide them with intelligence , agility , and a high energy level to perform a job ( wrangling sheep ) that they generally no longer have to do", "context_len": 46}}}, "rations": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "The convoy also delivered 137 vehicles , tents , aviation fuel , ammunition , rations and engineering equipment to Guadalcanal", "context_len": 20}}}, "unbroken": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "These new soldiers enabled Vandegrift , beginning on 19 September , to establish an unbroken defence around the Lunga perimeter", "context_len": 20}}}, "inflicted": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "The Marines inflicted caused a lot of deaths and wounding for the Japanese 4th Infantry Regiment", "context_len": 16}}}, "retreat": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 4, "context": "Allied ships had to retreat from the battle after one carrier was sunk ( ) and another ( ) heavily damaged", "context_len": 21}, "NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 41, "context": "Opening fire , Scott 's warships sank one of Got\u014d 's cruisers and one of his destroyers , heavily damaged another cruiser , seriously wounded Got\u014d , and forced the rest of Got\u014d 's warships to abandon the bombing mission and retreat", "context_len": 42}}}, "outposts": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "1st Battalion 2nd Marines attacked two small Japanese outposts about east of the Lunga perimeter at Gurabusu and Koilotumaria near Aola Bay", "context_len": 22}}}, "tenders": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Two seaplane tenders and six destroyers were to deliver 728 soldiers plus artillery and ammunition to Guadalcanal", "context_len": 17}}}, "battleships": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 19, "context": "In order to attack Kondo 's force , Halsey , who was low on undamaged ships , sent two battleships , and , and four destroyers from the `` Enterprise '' task force", "context_len": 33}}}, "bombard": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "To protect the approaching convoy from attack by CAF aircraft , Yamamoto sent two battleships from Truk to bombard Henderson Field", "context_len": 21}}}, "fragmentation": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Many of the shells were fragmentation shells , designed to destroy land targets", "context_len": 13}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "The two battleships , and , with special fragmentation shells , were to bomb Henderson Field on the night of 12\u201313 November and destroy it and the aircraft stationed there", "context_len": 30}}}, "mortars": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Marine and Army units armed with rifles , machine guns , mortars , and fire from 37 mm anti-tank guns did terrible damage to the Japanese", "context_len": 26}}}, "malnutrition": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 52, "context": "Research topics have included low crop and animal productivity , and environmental degradation , water management , fragile lands , property rights , collective action , sustainable intensification of agricultural production , the impact of climate change on poor farmers , the problems and opportunities of biotechnology , food security , micronutrient malnutrition , microfinance programs , urban food security , gender and development , and resource allocation within households", "context_len": 70}}}, "battled": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "The two opposing carrier forces battled each other on the morning of 26 October , in what became known as the Battle of the Santa Cruz Islands", "context_len": 27}}}, "aircrew": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 15, "context": "The Japanese carrier forces , however , also pulled back because of high aircraft and aircrew losses and major damage to two carriers", "context_len": 23}}}, "rejoin": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 10, "context": "Hyakutake ordered Sh\u014dji to leave his positions at Koli and rejoin Japanese forces at Kokumbona in the Matanikau area", "context_len": 19}}}, "retreating": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "During the patrol , Carlson 's soldierz fought several battles with Sh\u014dji 's retreating forces , killing almost 500 of them , while having 16 killed themselves", "context_len": 27}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "The Confederates started retreating when the center of their line was attacked by the 1st Kansas Colored Infantry", "context_len": 18}}}, "assemble": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Yamamoto ordered Nobutake Kond\u014d to assemble another bombing force using warships from Truk and Abe 's force to attack Henderson Field on 15 November", "context_len": 24}}}, "escorting": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Most of the troops were rescued from the transports by Tanaka 's escorting destroyers and returned to the Shortlands", "context_len": 19}}}, "undamaged": {"freq": 1, "POS"