 in the USA in the 1976 , the WAKO ( World Association of KickBoxing Organizations ) that had been founded in Germany in the 1978 ( WAKO has its origins in the organization of amateur gatherings ) , the ISKA ( that had been founded in 1986 ) that came from the PKA that did the development of the full contact at the beginning and the WKN ( that had been founded in the 1997 )", "context_len": 115}}}, "federations": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "International federations :", "context_len": 3}}}, "archerfish": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 1, "context": "The archerfish shoots drops of water out of its mouth at the insect", "context_len": 13}, "NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 4, "context": "There is the common archerfish , which has a similar common name but is not the type species", "context_len": 18}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "sooty": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "The body of the `` Toxotus chatareus '' sooty but sometimes silvery or gold", "context_len": 14}}}, "silvery": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "The body of the `` Toxotus chatareus '' sooty but sometimes silvery or gold", "context_len": 14}}}, "reputed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Their house was reputed a den of thieves", "context_len": 8}}}, "lad": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Bathurst-born Colonial lad John Peisley was eventually convicted of stealing cattle and sentenced to serve time on Cockatoo Island near Sydney , now called Biloela", "context_len": 25}}}, "escapee": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "There he met `` Darkie '' Frank Clark , who as Frank Christie , escapee from Melbourne \u2019 s Pentridge gaol in 1850 after serving five weeks of a five year sentence", "context_len": 32}}}, "forging": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "Convicted , he got seven years for attempting to sell stolen horses and forging horse ownership papers at Yass", "context_len": 19}}}, "absconded": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 5, "context": "Two months later , he absconded to new gold diggings at Kiandra and calling himself Frank Gardiner opened a butcher \u2019 s shop selling carcasses of stolen cattle", "context_len": 28}}}, "carcasses": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "Two months later , he absconded to new gold diggings at Kiandra and calling himself Frank Gardiner opened a butcher \u2019 s shop selling carcasses of stolen cattle", "context_len": 28}}}, "skipped": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "He was arrested in May 1861 , but skipped bail at Lambing Flat ( now Young )", "context_len": 17}}}, "ironbark": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "In May , at Fish River in Fogg \u2019 s ironbark slab humpy , six miles from Bigga , Peisley and Frank Clark reunited and teamed with John Gilbert as highway robbers , sticking up \u2019 travellers in the area between Bathurst , Lambing Flat , Gundagai and Yass", "context_len": 49}}}, "humpy": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "In May , at Fish River in Fogg \u2019 s ironbark slab humpy , six miles from Bigga , Peisley and Frank Clark reunited and teamed with John Gilbert as highway robbers , sticking up \u2019 travellers in the area between Bathurst , Lambing Flat , Gundagai and Yass", "context_len": 49}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "On 16 July morning , Sergeant John Middleton and Trooper William Hosie stationed at Tuena , descended upon Fogg \u2019 s humpy occupied by Fogg , his wife and children , Frank Clark armed with a six-shot revolver handgun , and Jim Barney , an old man", "context_len