 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "To find an explicit formula for the surface integral , mathematicians parametrize `` S '' by considering on `` S '' a system of curvilinear coordinates , like the latitude and longitude on a sphere", "context_len": 35}}}, "curvilinear": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "To find an explicit formula for the surface integral , mathematicians parametrize `` S '' by considering on `` S '' a system of curvilinear coordinates , like the latitude and longitude on a sphere", "context_len": 35}}}, "parametrization": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 13, "context": "If such a surface is split into pieces , on each piece a parametrization and corresponding surface normal is chosen , and the pieces are put back together , the normal vectors coming from different pieces can not be reconciled", "context_len": 40}}}, "tangent": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "This illustration implies that if the vector field is tangent to `` S '' at each point , then the flux is zero , because the fluid just flows in parallel to `` S '' , and neither in nor out", "context_len": 41}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "Where the two surfaces meet , they form a contact angle , formula 5 , which is the angle the tangent to the surface makes with the solid surface", "context_len": 29}}}, "generalization": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 24, "context": "Various useful results for surface integrals can be derived using differential geometry and vector calculus , such as the divergence theorem , and its generalization , Stokes ' theorem", "context_len": 29}}}, "normals": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 5, "context": "If , however , the normals for these parametrizations point in opposite directions , the value of the surface integral obtained using one parametrization is the negative of the one obtained via the other parametrization", "context_len": 35}}}, "cylinder": {"freq": 16, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 16, "word_index": 2, "context": "For the cylinder , this means that if we decide that for the side region the normal will point out of the body , then for the top and bottom circular parts , the normal must point out of the body too", "context_len": 42}}}, "reconciled": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 39, "context": "If such a surface is split into pieces , on each piece a parametrization and corresponding surface normal is chosen , and the pieces are put back together , the normal vectors coming from different pieces can not be reconciled", "context_len": 40}}}, "pointing": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 7, "context": "where formula 18 is the position vector pointing from the origin to the location of the volume element , and formula 19 is the current density vector at that location", "context_len": 30}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "These ambiguities are resolved by the right-hand rule : With the palm of the right-hand toward the area of integration , and the index-finger pointing along the direction of line-integration , the outstretched thumb points in the direction that must be chosen for the vector area dS", "context_len": 47}}}, "stele": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "The name comes from the orbiter name , already defined as Rosetta , which is the name of the stele that allowed Jean-Fran\u00e7ois Champollion to understand ancient Egypt hieroglyphics", "context_len": 29}}}, "hieroglyphics": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 28, "context": "The name comes from the orbiter name , already defined as Rosetta , which is the name of the stele that allowed Jean-Fran\u00e7ois Champollion to understand ancient Egypt hieroglyphics", "context_len": 29}}}, "brackets": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "in brackets : Level in Austrian football", "context_len": 7}}}, "clashes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "They were all but destroyed by settlement , disease brought by European settlers , and clashes with the settlers", "context_len": 19}}}, "centenary": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "The centenary of Local Government in Narrandera was celebrated in 1985", "context_len": 11}}}, "cereals": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "The MIA is a region where farmer grow rice and other cereals with irrigation , as well as citrus , wine grapes and potatoes", "context_len": 24}}}, "fig": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "The town also has number of historic attractions , such as a fig tree on the corner of King and Cadell Streets , which is thought to be 150 years old ; and the Mon Repos , a residence built in a Queen Anne-style , which was built in the 1890s", "context_len": 51}}}, "levee": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "The canal follows the natural bed of Bundidgerry Creek and in places is very wide and has no levee banks", "context_len": 20}}}, "groupings": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 2, "context": "Some older groupings ( `` high medium low income countries '' ) that have been removed were based on the gross domestic product ( GDP ) in purchasing power parity ( PPP ) per capita , and have been replaced by another index based on the gross national income ( GNI ) in purchasing power parity per capita", "context_len": 58}}}, "parity": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "asia": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Asia", "context_len": 1}}}, "intercontinental": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "List of countries by intercontinental region", "context_len": 6}}}, "infinitesimal": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 9, "context": "In differential calculus , in both the limit and infinitesimal versions , the velocity of a particle is represented by formula 1 , where `` s '' is the position of the particle and `` t '' the time at which the velocity is measured", "context_len": 45}}}, "outward": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "where E is the electric field and dA is a differential area on the surface formula 5 with an outward facing surface normal defining its direction", "context_len": 26}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Differences in the Sun 's magnetic field are carried outward by the solar wind and can produce magnetic storms in the Earth 's magnetosphere", "context_len": 24}}}, "volt": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 31, "context": "Weber ( unit of magnetic flux ) The weber is the magnetic flux which , linking a circuit of one turn , would produce in it an electromotive force of 1 volt if it were reduced to zero at a uniform rate in 1 second", "context_len": 45}}}, "equivalently": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 15, "context": "Electrical flux has SI units of volt metres ( V m ) , or , equivalently , newton metres squared per coulomb", "context_len": 22}}}, "newton": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 17, "context": "Electrical flux has SI units of volt metres ( V m ) , or , equivalently , newton metres squared per coulomb", "context_len": 22}}}, "squared": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "Electrical flux has SI units of volt metres ( V m ) , or , equivalently , newton metres squared per coulomb", "context_len": 22}}}, "coulomb": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 21, "context": "Electrical flux has SI units of volt metres ( V m ) , or , equivalently , newton metres squared per coulomb", "context_len": 22}}}, "brokered": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "He subsequently brokered an agreement with the Labour Party and formed a coalition government on 9 March 2011", "context_len": 18}}}, "antisemitism": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 18, "context": "The reason for this was that some players went to other clubs and some ended their career because antisemitism grew at that time", "context_len": 23}}}, "prolonged": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "The contract was not prolonged", "context_len": 5}}}, "alimentary": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "Gastroliths , or gizzard stones , are small rocks kept by an animal inside its stomach or at an early part of the alimentary canal", "context_len": 25}}}, "grinding": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 12, "context": "Typically , animals which do this do not have suitable teeth for grinding , and the gastroliths are a good substitute for this", "context_len": 23}}}, "ballast": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 12, "context": "Aquatic animals , such as plesiosaurs , may have used them as ballast , to help balance themselves or to decrease their buoyancy , as crocodiles do", "context_len": 27}}}, "gastrolith": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Secondly , it should be rounded and polished , because inside a gizzard any genuine gastrolith would grind against other stones and fibrous materials , like the action of a rock tumbler", "context_len": 32}}}, "fibrous": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 22, "context": "Secondly , it should be rounded and polished , because inside a gizzard any genuine gastrolith would grind against other stones and fibrous materials , like the action of a rock tumbler", "context_len": 32}}}, "tumbler": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 31, "context": "Secondly , it should be rounded and polished , because inside a gizzard any genuine gastrolith would grind against other stones and fibrous materials , like the action of a rock tumbler", "context_len": 32}}}, "ingested": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "Lastly , the stone must be found with the fossils of the animal which ingested it", "context_len": 16}}}, "ostriches": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Stones swallowed by ostriches can exceed a length of", "context_len": 9}}}, "ingest": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Amphibians such as the Axolotl ingest rocks that are presumed to be gastroliths", "context_len": 13}}}, "ingestion": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Ingestion of silt and gravel by tadpoles of various frog species improves buoyancy control", "context_len": 14}}}, "buoyancy": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 22, "context": "Aquatic animals , such as plesiosaurs , may have used them as ballast , to help balance themselves or to decrease their buoyancy , as crocodiles do", "context_len": 27}}}, "plesiosaurs": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Aquatic animals , such as plesiosaurs , may have used them as ballast , to help balance themselves or to decrease their buoyancy , as crocodiles do", "context_len": 27}}}, "kilograms": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 10, "context": "It measured about two meters in length and weighed 20 kilograms", "context_len": 11}}}, "scute": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "A scute is a bony external plate or scale , as on the shell of a turtle , the skin of crocodiles or the feet of some birds", "context_len": 28}}}, "scutes": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 15, "context": "Unlike the scales of fish and snakes , which are formed from the epidermis , scutes are formed in the lower vascular layer of the skin and the epidermal element is only the top surface", "context_len": 35}}}, "epidermal": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 28, "context": "Unlike the scales of fish and snakes , which are formed from the epidermis , scutes are formed in the lower vascular layer of the skin and the epidermal element is only the top surface", "context_len": 35}}}, "superficially": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 0, "context": "Superficially , neutron beamlines differ from synchrotron radiation beamlines mostly by the fact that they use neutrons from a research reactor or a spallation source instead of photons", "context_len": 28}}}, "dermal": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 4, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "armadillo": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 12, "context": "The term is also used to describe the heavy armour of the armadillo and the extinct glyptodon , and is occasionally used as an alternative to scales in describing snakes or certain fish , such as sturgeon", "context_len": 37}}}, "regeneration": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 23, "context": "It was a cone-shaped and it had several different places for radio transmitters , a telemetry system , a programming unit , a regeneration and temperature control system for the spacecraft , and scientific instruments", "context_len": 35}}}, "ankylosaur": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "The Nodosauridae is a family of ankylosaur dinosaurs , from Upper Jurassic to Upper Cretaceous strata of what are now North America , Asia , Antarctica and Europe", "context_len": 28}}}, "ankylosaurs": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 5, "context": "All nodosaurs , like other ankylosaurs , are medium-sized to large , heavily built quadrupedal herbivorous dinosaurs , with small denticulate teeth and rows of osteoderms ( a type of armour ) on the dorsolateral ( top and sides ) surfaces of the body", "context_len": 44}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "The clade Nodosauridae may be defined as `` all ankylosaurs closer to `` Panoplosaurus '' than to `` Ankylosaurus ''", "context_len": 20}}}, "denticulate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "All nodosaurs , like other ankylosaurs , are medium-sized to large , heavily built quadrupedal herbivorous dinosaurs , with small denticulate teeth and rows of osteoderms ( a type of armour ) on the dorsolateral ( top and sides ) surfaces of the body", "context_len": 44}}}, "inflected": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "French is moderately inflected", "context_len": 4}}}, "eu": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "However , if a noun ends in - '' au '' , - '' eu '' , or - '' ou '' , it can have - '' x '' at the end as a plural", "context_len": 36}}}, "auto": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "The very important industries are glass , ship making , Metallurgy ( making gold ) , and auto parts", "context_len": 19}}}, "wigglers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Wigglers make a wide range of electromagnetic radiation frequencies", "context_len": 9}}}, "spallation": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 38, "context": "In materials science , physics , chemistry , and molecular biology , a beamline leads to the experimental endstation utilizing particle beams from a particle accelerator , synchrotron light obtained from a synchrotron , or neutrons from a spallation source or research reactor", "context_len": 43}}}, "cased": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "In particle accelerators , the beamline is usually housed in a tunnel and or underground , cased inside a cement housing", "context_len": 21}}}, "align": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "A survey and alignment crew carefully align the beamline segments by using a laser tracker", "context_len": 15}}}, "crystallography": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 43, "context": "The Hanson Hall of Science 's facilities and resources include seven classrooms , thirty-five laboratories ( including a cadaver lab ) , a 400 MHz liquid-and solid-state NMR ( nuclear magnetic resonance ) spectrometer , scanning electron microscope , instrumentation for X-ray powder crystallography and a 40-foot greenhouse", "context_len": 48}}}, "optimized": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "A large synchrotron laboratory will have many beamlines , each optimized for a particular field of research", "context_len": 17}}}, "enclosures": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "The beamline elements are in radiation shielding enclosures , called hutches , which are the size of a small room ( cabin )", "context_len": 23}}}, "hutches": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 6, "context": "A typical beamline consists of two hutches , an optical hutch for the beam conditioning elements and an experimental hutch , which houses the experiment", "context_len": 25}}}, "hutch": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 18, "context": "Hutches have complex safety systems with redundant interlocking functions to make sure that no one is inside the hutch when the radiation is turned on", "context_len": 25}}}, "interlocking": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Hutches have complex safety systems with redundant interlocking functions to make sure that no one is inside the hutch when the radiation is turned on", "context_len": 25}}}, "dumping": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 9, "context": "Gingy starts first with a story about his girlfriend dumping him and asking the muffin man for a new girlfriend , made with loads of sugar , thus giving her the name Sugar as revealed in the credits", "context_len": 38}}}, "experimenters": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 0, "context": "Experimenters use the following elements that are used in beamlines for conditioning the radiation beam between the storage ring and the end station :", "context_len": 24}}}, "collimation": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 36, "context": "The combination of beam conditioning devices controls the thermal load ( heating caused by the beam ) at the end station ; the spectrum of radiation incident at the end station ; and the focus or collimation of the beam", "context_len": 40}}}, "ultra": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "The entire length of a beamline is normally kept under ultra high vacuum conditions", "context_len": 14}}}, "photons": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 27, "context": "Superficially , neutron beamlines differ from synchrotron radiation beamlines mostly by the fact that they use neutrons from a research reactor or a spallation source instead of photons", "context_len": 28}}}, "fred": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Fred Burton ( born January 2 , 1958 ) is STATFOR 's vice president for intelligence", "context_len": 16}}}, "mastermind": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 16, "context": "The next morning , Norbit is locked in the basement by Rasputia , who is the mastermind of the orphanage plot and had her brothers carry it out", "context_len": 28}}}, "collinear": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "The word `` collimated '' is related to `` collinear '' , because all the rays in collimated light line up with each other", "context_len": 24}}}, "diffraction": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Diffraction prevents anyone from creating a perfectly collimated beam", "context_len": 9}}}, "collimator": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Light can be roughly collimated by using a `` collimator '' \u2013 a device which narrows a beam of particles or waves", "context_len": 22}}}, "narrows": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Light can be roughly collimated by using a `` collimator '' \u2013 a device which narrows a beam of particles or waves", "context_len": 22}}}, "collimate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "The word `` collimate '' comes from the Latin verb `` collimare '' , which originated in a misreading of `` collineare '' , `` to direct in a straight line ''", "context_len": 32}}}, "misreading": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "The word `` collimate '' comes from the Latin verb `` collimare '' , which originated in a misreading of `` collineare '' , `` to direct in a straight line ''", "context_len": 32}}}, "diodes": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Laser diodes emit less collimated light due to their short cavity , and therefore higher collimation requires a collimating lens", "context_len": 20}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "Light-emitting diodes are devices that often use phosphors to obtain a particular color or color temperature", "context_len": 16}}}, "collimating": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "Laser diodes emit less collimated light due to their short cavity , and therefore higher collimation requires a collimating lens", "context_len": 20}}}, "conversely": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Conversely , a point source at the focus of a parabolic mirror will produce a beam of collimated light", "context_len": 19}}}, "resets": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "The bill amends the Civil Rights Act of 1964 stating that the 180-day statute of limitations for filing an equal-pay lawsuit regarding pay discrimination resets with each new discriminatory paycheck", "context_len": 30}}}, "discriminatory": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 24, "context": "Supreme Court decision holding that the statute of limitations for presenting an equal-pay lawsuit begins on the date that the employer makes the initial discriminatory wage decision , not at the date of the most recent paycheck , as a lower court had ruled", "context_len": 44}, "UNK": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 21, "context": "The Supreme Court ruled in 2007 by a 5-4 majority vote that Ledbetter 's complaint was filed too late because the discriminatory decisions relating to pay had been made more than 180 days prior to the date she filed her charge , as explained by Justice Samuel Alito", "context_len": 48}}}, "amend": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "A first bill to amend the statutory limitations period and supersede the `` Ledbetter '' decision was introduced in the 110th United States Congress but was never enacted , as after having been passed by the House it failed to survive a cloture vote in the Senate due to the opposition of most of the Republican Senators", "context_len": 57}}}, "cloture": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 42, "context": "A first bill to amend the statutory limitations period and supersede the `` Ledbetter '' decision was introduced in the 110th United States Congress but was never enacted , as after having been passed by the House it failed to survive a cloture vote in the Senate due to the opposition of most of the Republican Senators", "context_len": 57}}}, "setback": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 14, "context": "It was seen as another high-profile British millennium project that had suffered an embarrassing setback , similar to how many saw the Millennium Dome", "context_len": 24}}}, "clarion": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 46, "context": "Among the first to criticize the Court 's decision was Marcia Greenberger , president of the National Women 's Law Center , that saw in the ruling a `` setback for women and a setback for civil rights '' and called Ginsburg 's opinion a `` clarion call to the American people that this slim majority of the court is headed in the wrong direction", "context_len": 65}}}, "eliminates": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 28, "context": "On the other side , the majority 's findings were applauded by the US Chamber of Commerce , that called it a `` fair decision '' that `` eliminates a potential wind-fall against employers by employees trying to dredge up stale pay claims", "context_len": 43}}}, "dredge": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 38, "context": "On the other side , the majority 's findings were applauded by the US Chamber of Commerce , that called it a `` fair decision '' that `` eliminates a potential wind-fall against employers by employees trying to dredge up stale pay claims", "context_len": 43}}}, "intervene": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 28, "context": "Claiming lead from Justice Ruth Ginsburg 's minority opinion , which invited the Congress to take action by amending the law , the Democrats announced their intention to intervene : House Majority Leader Steny Hoyer and Education and Labor Committee Chairman George Miller said that a bill was to be passed to avoid future court rulings in line with `` Ledbetter '' , clearly putting that `` a key provision of the legislation will make it clear that discrimination occurs not just when the decision to discriminate is made , but also when someone becomes subject to that discriminatory decision , and when they are affected by that discriminatory decision , including each time they are issued a discriminatory paycheck '' , as said by Rep", "context_len": 126}}}, "loophole": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 49, "context": "Republicans immediately opposed the bill as drafted , with Education and Labor Committee ranking member Howard McKeon raising the issue that companies would be held liable for actions taken by managers who were not leading the company anymore : `` At the end of the day , such a loophole conceivably could allow a retiring employee to seek damages against a company now led by executives who had nothing to do with the initial act of discrimination ''", "context_len": 78}}}, "conceivably": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 50, "context": "Republicans immediately opposed the bill as drafted , with Education and Labor Committee ranking member Howard McKeon raising the issue that companies would be held liable for actions taken by managers who were not leading the company anymore : `` At the end of the day , such a loophole conceivably could allow a retiring employee to seek damages against a company now led by executives who had nothing to do with the initial act of discrimination ''", "context_len": 78}}}, "nay": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 38, "context": "The vote was nearly perfectly split along party lines , with only three Republicans voting in favor ( Ed Whitfield of Kentucky , Don Young of Alaska and Chris Smith of New Jersey ) and three Democrats voting nay ( Travis Childers of Mississippi , Allen Boyd of Florida , and Parker Griffith of Alabama )", "context_len": 56}}}, "nullify": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "It was the first act he signed as president , and it fulfilled his campaign pledge to nullify `` Ledbetter v", "context_len": 21}}}, "communicates": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "Collective animal behaviour is about finding the rules each animal follows ; how it communicates with other members of the group and how a decision to do something is reached in the group", "context_len": 33}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 37, "context": "The International Council of Museums defines a `` museum '' as a `` permanent institution in the service of society and of its development , open to the public , which acquires , conserves , researches , communicates , and exhibits the tangible and intangible heritage of humanity and its environment , for the purposes of education , study , and enjoyment ''", "context_len": 63}}}, "productivity": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "Research topics have included low crop and animal productivity , and environmental degradation , water management , fragile lands , property rights , collective action , sustainable intensification of agricultural production , the impact of climate change on poor farmers , the problems and opportunities of biotechnology , food security , micronutrient malnutrition , microfinance programs , urban food security , gender and development , and resource allocation within households", "context_len": 70}}}, "micronutrient": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 51, "context": "Research topics have included low crop and animal productivity , and environmental degradation , water management , fragile lands , property rights , collective action , sustainable intensification of agricultural production , the impact of climate change on poor farmers , the problems and opportunities of biotechnology , food security , micronutrient malnutrition , microfinance programs , urban food security , gender and development , and resource allocation within households", "context_len": 70}}}, "analyzes": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 2, "context": "IFPRI also analyzes agricultural market reforms , trade policy , World Trade Organization negotiations in the context of agriculture , institutional effectiveness , crop and income diversification , postharvest activity , and agroindustry", "context_len": 33}}}, "newsletters": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "IFPRI publishes books , research reports , but also newsletters , briefs , and fact sheets", "context_len": 16}}}, "briefs": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "IFPRI publishes books , research reports , but also newsletters , briefs , and fact sheets", "context_len": 16}}}, "extravagant": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 30, "context": "Whilst event centre rock has seen large popularity over the years , especially from the 1960s to the 1980s , it has also been criticised for its often commercial and extravagant nature , especially with regards to the shows and concert tours that event centre rock bands and artists would have", "context_len": 51}}}, "opting": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 32, "context": "To some extent , genres such as pub rock , punk rock , indie rock and alternative rock grew as a reaction against the nature and aesthetic of event centre rock , opting for a less commercial and over-the-top style", "context_len": 40}}}, "scapegoat": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "They believe that Ray was a scapegoat", "context_len": 7}}}, "cheek": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "The bullet entered through his right cheek , and travelled down his neck", "context_len": 13}}}, "massaged": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Doctors cut open his chest and massaged his heart to try to keep blood and oxygen pumping through his body", "context_len": 20}}}, "pumping": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "Doctors cut open his chest and massaged his heart to try to keep blood and oxygen pumping through his body", "context_len": 20}}}, "penitentiary": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "On March 10 , 1969 , Ray told the court he was guilty , and was sentenced to 99 years in the Tennessee state penitentiary", "context_len": 25}}}, "recommends": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "The investigation report recommends no more investigation unless some reliable new facts are presented", "context_len": 14}}}, "sabotaging": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "His activities sabotaging French occupying troops after World War I led to his arrest and eventual execution by French forces", "context_len": 20}}}, "reluctance": {"freq": 14, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 14, "word_index": 29, "context": "As an electric field causes an electric current to follow the path of least resistance , a magnetic field causes magnetic flux to follow the path of least magnetic reluctance", "context_len": 30}}}, "dissipating": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 17, "context": "After extensive analysis by the engineers , the problem was fixed by fitting 37 dampers ( energy dissipating ) to control horizontal movement and 52 ( inertial ) dampers to control vertical movement", "context_len": 33}}}, "magnetomotive": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "The total reluctance is equal to the ratio of the `` magnetomotive force ( MMF ) in a passive magnetic circuit to the magnetic flux in this circuit", "context_len": 28}}}, "rowland": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Rowland", "context_len": 1}}}, "sinusoidal": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "If the perturbations are resolved into sinusoidal components , we find that some components grow with time while others decay with time", "context_len": 22}}}, "inductance": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 26, "context": "If the rate of change of current in a circuit is one ampere per second and the resulting electromotive force is one volt , then the inductance of the circuit is one henry", "context_len": 33}}}, "circuital": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 2, "context": "Amp\u00e8re 's circuital law is now known to be a correct law of physics in a magnetostatic situation : The system is static except possibly for continuous steady currents within closed loops", "context_len": 32}}}, "ambiguities": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 10, "context": "First , three of these terms are associated with sign ambiguities : the line integral formula 5 could go around the loop in either direction ( clockwise or counterclockwise ) ; the vector area dS could point in either of the two directions normal to the surface ; and `` I '' enc is the net current passing through the surface `` S '' , meaning the current passing through in one direction , minus the current in the other direction but either direction could be chosen as positive", "context_len": 89}}}, "clarification": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "There are a number of ambiguities in the above definitions that require clarification and a choice of convention", "context_len": 18}}}, "counterclockwise": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 28, "context": "First , three of these terms are associated with sign ambiguities : the line integral formula 5 could go around the loop in either direction ( clockwise or counterclockwise ) ; the vector area dS could point in either of the two directions normal to the surface ; and `` I '' enc is the net current passing through the surface `` S '' , meaning the current passing through in one direction , minus the current in the other direction but either direction could be chosen as positive", "context_len": 89}}}, "outstretched": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 32, "context": "These ambiguities are resolved by the right-hand rule : With the palm of the right-hand toward the area of integration , and the index-finger pointing along the direction of line-integration , the outstretched thumb points in the direction that must be chosen for the vector area dS", "context_len": 47}}}, "arises": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "The electric current that arises in the simplest textbook situations would be classified as `` free current", "context_len": 17}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "In contrast , `` bound current '' arises in the context of bulk materials that can be magnetized and or polarized", "context_len": 21}}}, "perpetually": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 22, "context": "When the currents from all these atoms are put together , they create the same effect as a macroscopic current , circulating perpetually around the magnetized object", "context_len": 27}}}, "polarizable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "When an electric field is applied , the positive and negative bound charges can separate over atomic distances in polarizable materials , and when the bound charges move , the polarization changes , creating another contribution to the `` bound current '' , the polarization current JP", "context_len": 47}}}, "microscopically": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "All current is fundamentally the same , microscopically", "context_len": 8}}}, "densities": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 15, "context": "In both forms J includes magnetization current density as well as conduction and polarization current densities", "context_len": 16}}}, "propagation": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 32, "context": "The displacement current is justified today because it serves several requirements of an electromagnetic theory : correct prediction of magnetic fields in regions where no free current flows ; prediction of wave propagation of electromagnetic fields ; and conservation of electric charge in cases where charge density is time-varying", "context_len": 49}}}, "permittivity": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "where 0 is the electric constant , `` '' r the relative static permittivity , and P is the polarization density", "context_len": 21}}}, "substituting": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 26, "context": "The above equation can be used for calculating a magnetic moment of any assembly of moving charges , such as a spinning charged solid , by substituting", "context_len": 27}}}, "justified": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "The displacement current is justified today because it serves several requirements of an electromagnetic theory : correct prediction of magnetic fields in regions where no free current flows ; prediction of wave propagation of electromagnetic fields ; and conservation of electric charge in cases where charge density is time-varying", "context_len": 49}, "VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 18, "context": "The Zen priest Brian Daizen Victoria wrote in his book `` Zen at War '' that Buddhist groups justified Japanese militarism", "context_len": 21}}}, "remedying": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Amp\u00e8re 's equation was extended by including the polarization current , thereby remedying the limited applicability of the original Amp\u00e8re 's circuital law", "context_len": 23}}}, "applicability": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Amp\u00e8re 's equation was extended by including the polarization current , thereby remedying the limited applicability of the original Amp\u00e8re 's circuital law", "context_len": 23}}}, "footing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "On the other hand , treating all charges on the same footing ( disregarding whether they are bound or free charges ) , the generalized Amp\u00e8re 's equation ( also called the Maxwell\u2013Amp\u00e8re equation ) is ( see the `` proof '' section below ) :", "context_len": 46}}}, "disregarding": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "On the other hand , treating all charges on the same footing ( disregarding whether they are bound or free charges ) , the generalized Amp\u00e8re 's equation ( also called the Maxwell\u2013Amp\u00e8re equation ) is ( see the `` proof '' section below ) :", "context_len": 46}}}, "hypothesize": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "With the addition of the displacement current , Maxwell was able to hypothesize ( correctly ) that light was a form of electromagnetic wave", "context_len": 24}}}, "iliac": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Coming from the heart the blood flows along the iliac artery which then divides into the two ( bifurcates ) femoral arteries , to supply blood to each leg", "context_len": 29}}}, "bifurcates": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "Coming from the heart the blood flows along the iliac artery which then divides into the two ( bifurcates ) femoral arteries , to supply blood to each leg", "context_len": 29}}}, "intestinal": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "It is based on the ecosystem in the human intestinal system", "context_len": 11}}}, "guts": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Research shows there are three distinct ecosystems in the guts of people", "context_len": 12}}}, "kissogram": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "She is working as a kissogram", "context_len": 6}}}, "jitters": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Because of `` pre-wedding jitters '' , she tries to seduce him", "context_len": 12}}}, "centurion": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 10, "context": ", As she remembers , it is shown that the centurion Rory is only an Auton living plastic that looks and acts like Rory", "context_len": 24}}}, "rory": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 0, "context": "Rory Williams is a fictional character in the British science fiction television series `` Doctor Who ''", "context_len": 17}, "NOUN": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 0, "context": "Rory and Amy learn that their daughter is River Song , and become related to the Doctor when he marries River in The Wedding of River Song", "context_len": 27}}}, "bluest": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "He tells her that it is `` old and new , '' and `` big and small '' and `` the bluest blue that there is ''", "context_len": 27}}}, "wakes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Amy wakes up on her wedding day and is reunited with her parents", "context_len": 13}}}, "dreaming": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "The woman keeps saying that `` she must be dreaming ''", "context_len": 11}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "based on ideas of lucid dreaming and dream incubation", "context_len": 9}}}, "avatar": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "In `` The Almost People '' it is shown that the Amy with the Doctor is actually an avatar version", "context_len": 20}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "She is a `` Flesh '' avatar", "context_len": 7}}}, "regenerates": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "When adult Mels ( Nina Toussaint-White ) is shot , she regenerates into her next form ( Kingston ) and kills the Doctor", "context_len": 23}}}, "perfume": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 25, "context": "In the now-fixed ( main ) timeline , Rory and Amy are still married and Amy has become a model spokeswoman for a line of perfume", "context_len": 26}}}, "heartbreaking": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "In December 2011 , the BBC 's Steven Moffat confirmed that Amy and Rory would be leaving the series in 2012 in `` heartbreaking '' circumstances", "context_len": 26}}}, "soothsayer": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Gillan was a soothsayer in the episode `` The Fires of Pompeii ''", "context_len": 13}}}, "incredible": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 4, "context": "Matt Smith is an incredible actor and it is going to be so much fun to act alongside him \u2013 I just ca n't wait to get started", "context_len": 28}}}, "outspoken": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "Executive producer Piers Wenger said that Amy was meant to be `` feisty and outspoken and a bit of a number", "context_len": 21}, "VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 3, "context": "Talai has been outspoken on social media in regard to racism , misogyny , gun control , worker \u2019 s rights , and other issues", "context_len": 25}}}, "wildest": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Amy is probably the wildest companion that the Doctor has travelled with , but she isn \u2019 t promiscuous", "context_len": 19}}}, "binder": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 23, "context": "It consists of marble , quartz , granite , glass or other suitable chips , sprinkled or unsprinkled , and poured with a binder that is cement-like , chemical or a combination of both", "context_len": 34}}}, "precast": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "It is poured in place or precast", "context_len": 7}}}, "sprinkled": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 15, "context": "It consists of marble , quartz , granite , glass or other suitable chips , sprinkled or unsprinkled , and poured with a binder that is cement-like , chemical or a combination of both", "context_len": 34}}}, "uniformly": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "Sometimes , it is finished to produce a uniformly textured surface that is not flat", "context_len": 15}}}, "textured": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Sometimes , it is finished to produce a uniformly textured surface that is not flat", "context_len": 15}}}, "artisans": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "Terrazzo artisans create walkways , floors , patios , and panels by exposing marble chips and other fine aggregates on the surface of finished concrete or epoxy-resin", "context_len": 27}}}, "patios": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 7, "context": "Terrazzo artisans create walkways , floors , patios , and panels by exposing marble chips and other fine aggregates on the surface of finished concrete or epoxy-resin", "context_len": 27}}}, "aggregates": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 18, "context": "Terrazzo artisans create walkways , floors , patios , and panels by exposing marble chips and other fine aggregates on the surface of finished concrete or epoxy-resin", "context_len": 27}}}, "terrazzo": {"freq": 27, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 5, "context": "For the final layer , terrazzo workers blend and place into each of the panels a fine marble chip mixture that may be color-pigmented", "context_len": 24}, "NOUN": {"freq": 20, "word_index": 19, "context": "Consisting originally of marble chips , clay , and goat milk ( as the sealer ) , production of terrazzo became much easier after the 1920s and the introduction of electric industrial grinders and other power equipment", "context_len": 37}}}, "embed": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 8, "context": "Before this layer sets , terrazzo workers partially embed metal divider strips in the concrete wherever there is to be a joint or change of color in the terrazzo", "context_len": 29}}}, "divider": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 10, "context": "Before this layer sets , terrazzo workers partially embed metal divider strips in the concrete wherever there is to be a joint or change of color in the terrazzo", "context_len": 29}}}, "toss": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "While the mixture is still wet , workers toss additional marble chips of various colors into each panel and roll a lightweight roller over the entire surface", "context_len": 27}}}, "ester": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Initially polyester and vinyl ester resins were used as the binder resin", "context_len": 12}}}, "impermeable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "95 cm ) installation thickness , lighter weight , faster installation , impermeable finish , higher strength , and cracking less", "context_len": 21}}}, "abalone": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "In addition to marble aggregate blends , other aggregates have been used such as mother of pearl and abalone shell", "context_len": 20}}}, "medallions": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Shapes and medallions can be fabricated on site by bending divider strips or off site by water-jet cutting", "context_len": 18}}}, "polisher": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 31, "context": "When the terrazzo is thoroughly dry ( or cured in the case of thin-set terrazzo ) , helpers grind it with a terrazzo grinder , which is somewhat like a floor polisher , only much heavier", "context_len": 36}}}, "grout": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "Slight depressions left by the grinding are filled with a matching grout material and hand-troweled for a smooth , uniform surface", "context_len": 21}}}, "contractors": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Terrazzo contractors then clean , polish , and seal the dry surface for a finish that shines", "context_len": 17}}}, "venetian": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Venetian construction workers invented terrazzo for use as a low cost flooring material using leftover marble chips from upscale jobs", "context_len": 20}}}, "sealer": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "Consisting originally of marble chips , clay , and goat milk ( as the sealer ) , production of terrazzo became much easier after the 1920s and the introduction of electric industrial grinders and other power equipment", "context_len": 37}}}, "grinders": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 32, "context": "Consisting originally of marble chips , clay , and goat milk ( as the sealer ) , production of terrazzo became much easier after the 1920s and the introduction of electric industrial grinders and other power equipment", "context_len": 37}}}, "neolithic": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 13, "context": "Archaeologists use the word `` terrazzo '' to describe the floors of early neolithic buildings ( PPN A and B , ca", "context_len": 22}}}, "ochre": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "9,000\u20138,000 BC ) in Western Asia , that are constructed of burnt lime and clay , colored red with ochre and polished", "context_len": 22}}}, "mottled": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "The embedded crushed limestone gives it a slightly mottled appearance", "context_len": 10}}}, "binders": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 1, "context": "The binders constitute 25-30 percent of the volume of a floor ; the remainder is composed of aggregates , pigments and fillers", "context_len": 22}}}, "refinished": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Terrazzo flooring can be refinished repeatedly , reusing instead of replacing materials", "context_len": 12}}}, "refinishing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "Even century-old floors have generally proven need little more than minor repairs and refinishing to return them to their original beauty", "context_len": 21}}}, "mopping": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Routine maintenance should be no more than dry and damp mopping , with an occasional spray buffing", "context_len": 17}}}, "buffing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "Routine maintenance should be no more than dry and damp mopping , with an occasional spray buffing", "context_len": 17}}}, "waxing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Waxing or chemical cleaners only serve to cloud or damage the finish", "context_len": 12}}}, "stripping": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Annual stripping and resealing can be done with water-based products", "context_len": 10}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "They form bands as nymphs and swarms as adults both of which can travel great distances , rapidly stripping fields and greatly damaging crops", "context_len": 24}}}, "resealing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Annual stripping and resealing can be done with water-based products", "context_len": 10}}}, "fillers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "The binders constitute 25-30 percent of the volume of a floor ; the remainder is composed of aggregates , pigments and fillers", "context_len": 22}}}, "microbial": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "A microbial cyst is a resting or dormant stage of a microorganism , usually a bacterium or a protist or rarely an invertebrate animal , that helps the organism to survive in unfavorable environmental conditions", "context_len": 35}}}, "sourcing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "The potential for local sourcing is another environmental strength of Terrazzo", "context_len": 11}}}, "realistically": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "On typical projects , Terrazzo can realistically contribute to five LEED credits : MRcr4 ( 2 ) , MRcr5 ( 2 ) EQcr4 ( 1 )", "context_len": 26}}}, "permeability": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": ") The magnetic permeability of a complete vacuum is 4 10 7 H m ( henry per meter )", "context_len": 19}}}, "henries": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "The National Institute of Standards and Technology provides guidance for American users of SI to write the plural as henries", "context_len": 20}}}, "capitalize": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "People do not capitalize unit names", "context_len": 6}}}, "ampere": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 31, "context": "Many times , the weber is expressed in terms of other derived units as the Tesla-square meter ( T m2 ) , volt-seconds ( V s ) , or joules per ampere ( J A )", "context_len": 36}}}, "electromotive": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 27, "context": "Weber ( unit of magnetic flux ) The weber is the magnetic flux which , linking a circuit of one turn , would produce in it an electromotive force of 1 volt if it were reduced to zero at a uniform rate in 1 second", "context_len": 45}}}, "joule": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "& lt ; br & gt ; J joule", "context_len": 9}}}, "weber": {"freq": 9, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 4, "context": "Many times , the weber is expressed in terms of other derived units as the Tesla-square meter ( T m2 ) , volt-seconds ( V s ) , or joules per ampere ( J A )", "context_len": 36}