"POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "In a concurring opinion , Michigan Supreme Court Judge Thomas M", "context_len": 11}}}, "expressly": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 43, "context": "In `` Municipal Corporations '' ( 1872 ) , Dillon explained that in contrast to the powers of states , which are unlimited but for express restrictions under the state or federal constitution , municipalities only have the powers that the state legislature expressly gives to them", "context_len": 47}}}, "indispensable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 37, "context": "It says that municipal governments only have the powers that are expressly granted to them by the state legislature , those that are necessarily implied from that grant of power , and those that are essential and indispensable to the municipality 's existence and functioning", "context_len": 45}}}, "discretion": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "However , when the state has not specifically directed the method by which the municipality may implement its granted power , the municipality has the discretion to choose the method so long as its choice is reasonable", "context_len": 37}}}, "imposes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Critics of the rule say that it imposes unreasonable constraints on the ability of communities to govern themselves and so undermines democracy , and even that local self-government is a matter of natural right that does not need to be conferred by higher political structures", "context_len": 45}}}, "unreasonable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "Critics of the rule say that it imposes unreasonable constraints on the ability of communities to govern themselves and so undermines democracy , and even that local self-government is a matter of natural right that does not need to be conferred by higher political structures", "context_len": 45}}}, "constraints": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 9, "context": "Critics of the rule say that it imposes unreasonable constraints on the ability of communities to govern themselves and so undermines democracy , and even that local self-government is a matter of natural right that does not need to be conferred by higher political structures", "context_len": 45}}}, "undermines": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "Critics of the rule say that it imposes unreasonable constraints on the ability of communities to govern themselves and so undermines democracy , and even that local self-government is a matter of natural right that does not need to be conferred by higher political structures", "context_len": 45}}}, "inherently": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "It has also been suggested that Dillon 's approach came from the view at that time that cities were inherently corrupt political organs", "context_len": 23}}}, "alter": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 7, "context": "The Court 's ruling that states could alter or abolish at will the charters of municipal corporations without infringing upon contract rights relied upon Dillon 's separation of public , municipal corporations from private ones", "context_len": 35}}}, "charters": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 13, "context": "The Court 's ruling that states could alter or abolish at will the charters of municipal corporations without infringing upon contract rights relied upon Dillon 's separation of public , municipal corporations from private ones", "context_len": 35}}}, "infringing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 18, "context": "The Court 's ruling that states could alter or abolish at will the charters of municipal corporations without infringing upon contract rights relied upon Dillon 's separation of public , municipal corporations from private ones", "context_len": 35}}}, "rawlings": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 0, "context": "Rawlings began initiatives in certain areas of science and engineering that he considered important to the future ( such as bioinformatics , computational biology , computer and information sciences , genomics , and materials science ) , and began plans for Weill Hall , a large new life sciences building", "context_len": 50}}}, "manslaughter": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Italian prosecutors charged six people with manslaughter in connection with Senna 's death , all of whom were later found to be not guilty", "context_len": 24}}}, "tyre": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 39, "context": "At the drivers ' briefing before the race , Senna , along with Gerhard Berger , had expressed concern that the safety car ( which only came into F1 in 1993 ) did not go fast enough to keep tyre temperatures high", "context_len": 42}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "During this period , as a result of going at slower speeds , tyre temperatures dropped", "context_len": 16}}}, "brushed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 29, "context": "Ten years after the incident , Damon Hill , who drove for the Williams-Renault team at the time , described the feeling after the crash : `` We all brushed ourselves off and carried on qualifying , reassured that our cars were tough as tanks and we could be shaken but not hurt", "context_len": 53}}}, "reassured": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 37, "context": "Ten years after the incident , Damon Hill , who drove for the Williams-Renault team at the time , described the feeling after the crash : `` We all brushed ourselves off and carried on qualifying , reassured that our cars were tough as tanks and we could be shaken but not hurt", "context_len": 53}}}, "briefing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1,