s the first unmanned test flight mission of the Saturn V launch vehicle", "context_len": 15}}}, "spacesuit": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "He was the first American to take a `` spacewalk , '' leaving the safety of his spaceship while in space and moving around outside in a spacesuit", "context_len": 28}}}, "spark": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 19, "context": "The amount of flammable material , when mixed with the pure oxygen in the spacecraft , only needed a spark to start a serious fire", "context_len": 25}}}, "adventurous": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "In 1607 , Pocahontas , a Native American , likes to be adventurous with her friend , Nacoma , and her animal friends", "context_len": 23}}}, "pocahontas": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 0, "context": "Pocahontas then shares her knowledge and shows Smith that family values , life and nature are the most important things then having a king and buildings ( `` Colors of The Wind '' )", "context_len": 34}}}, "offended": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Pocahontas is offended when Smith calls her people `` savages '' because they do not have any modern buildings or a society ruled by a king", "context_len": 26}}}, "savages": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 9, "context": "Pocahontas is offended when Smith calls her people `` savages '' because they do not have any modern buildings or a society ruled by a king", "context_len": 26}}}, "shogun": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 4, "context": "was a general and shogun of the early Heian Period of Japan", "context_len": 12}}}, "quiver": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "His bow , arrows , quiver and sword were buried with him by order of the Emperor", "context_len": 17}}}, "inlet": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "The original Ithaca Municipal Airport was located west of downtown Ithaca , near the inlet of Cayuga Lake", "context_len": 18}}}, "crowded": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "The airport was hurt by the small size of the market , relative proximity to Syracuse Hancock International Airport and other regional airports , and crowded conditions in Northeastern airspace", "context_len": 30}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "It also let units get ready for deployments away from the crowded base there", "context_len": 14}}}, "nonstop": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 2, "context": "US Airways nonstop service to Pittsburgh resumed on November 9 , 2005 but stopped again on April 1 , 2006 due to low use", "context_len": 24}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "On 13 October , the record-making Truculent Turtle , which had flown nonstop for almost 4,500 miles , paid the station a visit", "context_len": 23}}}, "ultralight": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 26, "context": "At that time there were 62 aircraft based at this airport : 68 % single-engine , 15 % multi-engine , 16 % jet and 2 % ultralight", "context_len": 27}}}, "curves": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 21, "context": "He was known for varying his style according to the demands of the project : simple , sweeping , arching structural curves or machine-like rationalism", "context_len": 25}}}, "eclipsing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Examples are eclipsing binaries and cepheid variables", "context_len": 7}}}, "cepheid": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Examples are eclipsing binaries and cepheid variables", "context_len": 7}}}, "aperiodic": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Light curves can also be aperiodic , that is they are irregular with no pattern", "context_len": 15}}}, "nova": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Examples include the light curve of a nova , a cataclysmic variable star , a supernova or other event", "context_len": 19}}}, "constrains": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 22, "context": "The study of the light curve , together with other observations , gives information about the physical process that produces it or constrains the physical theories about it", "context_len": 28}}}, "photosynthetic": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "In botany , a light curve shows the photosynthetic response of a leaf or algae to the brightness of a light", "context_len": 21}}}, "saturation": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "The point on the graph where these two differing lines meet is called the light saturation point", "context_len": 17}}}, "nautical": {"freq": 9, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 9, "word_index": 9, "context": "Long Beach Airport is a city-owned public-use airport three nautical miles ( 6 km ) northeast of the central business district of the City of Long Beach , in Los Angeles County , California , United States", "context_len": 37}}}, "ligaments": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Open fractures can also damage muscles , tendons and ligaments if the sharp ends of the broken bone go through them", "context_len": 21}}}, "comminuted": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "In a `` comminuted '' fracture , at least three pieces of a bone have broken off", "context_len": 17}}}, "prescribe": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "To help decrease pain from the fracture , doctors can prescribe medications or suggest over-the-counter painkillers", "context_len": 16}}}, "painkillers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "To help decrease pain from the fracture , doctors can prescribe medications or suggest over-the-counter painkillers", "context_len": 16}}}, "pendulum": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "For example , a pendulum in a clock moves from some position ( called its `` displacement '' ) to the left ( labelled -x with algebra ) , to the bottom , and then to some position to the right ( labelled x with algebra )", "context_len": 47}}}, "pendulums": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Two pendulums may have the same length , but unless they begin swinging at the same time and place they will not move together", "context_len": 24}}}, "pointedly": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Smith pointedly requested that the city of Long Beach repair the runways and reminded the city that the Pacific Fleet , then laying offshore in both Long Beach and San Pedro harbors , had a payroll of more than $ 1 million a month", "context_len": 44}}}, "payroll": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 35, "context": "Smith pointedly requested that the city of Long Beach repair the runways and reminded the city that the Pacific Fleet , then laying offshore in both Long Beach and San Pedro harbors , had a payroll of more than $ 1 million a month", "context_len": 44}}}, "complied": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Eventually the city complied with the Navy 's requests", "context_len": 9}}}, "plywood": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 33, "context": "By the end of the year , the base 's 36 planes had increased to 140 , and in 1943 , five outlying fields were acquired , Training was carried out mostly in plywood planes", "context_len": 35}}}, "dispatched": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "Many CASUs and ARGUSs ( groups to establish forward air bases ) were formed at and dispatched from Los Alamitos during the war", "context_len": 23}}}, "reclassified": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "On 15 August 1943 it became an operational training base for training of fleet units and was reclassified as a Naval Air Station", "context_len": 23}}}, "reservists": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 6, "word_index": 10, "context": "Meanwhile , in answer to President Truman 's request for reservists to volunteer for duty during the Korean War , VG-781 requested mobilization as a complete unit , and was accepted \u2013 the first squadron in the nation to do so", "context_len": 41}}}, "madhouses": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Operations were limited on Mondays and Thursdays ; weekends were madhouses as the `` weekend warriors '' came on board", "context_len": 20}}}, "supersonic": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "Project Bullet , as the mission was called , provided both the first transcontinental flight to average supersonic speed , and the first continuous transcontinental panoramic photograph of the United States", "context_len": 31}}}, "panoramic": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 25, "context": "Project Bullet , as the mission was called , provided both the first transcontinental flight to average supersonic speed , and the first continuous transcontinental panoramic photograph of the United States", "context_len": 31}}}, "flagpole": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "The senior command on post is the 40th Infantry Division ( Mechanized ) , headquartered in the large , prominent building facing the flagpole and main entrance artery", "context_len": 28}}}, "outreach": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 45, "context": "Its mission is `` to provide forefront scientific facilities , opportunities and leadership essential for discovering the fundamental structure of nuclear matter ; to partner in industry to apply its advanced technology ; and to serve the nation and its communities through education and public outreach", "context_len": 46}}}, "injector": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "The laboratory 's main research facility is the CEBAF accelerator , which consists of a polarized electron source and injector and a pair of 7 8 mile ( 1400 m ) long superconducting RF linear accelerators", "context_len": 36}}}, "superconducting": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 32, "context": "The laboratory 's main research facility is the CEBAF accelerator , which consists of a polarized electron source and injector and a pair of 7 8 mile ( 1400 m ) long superconducting RF linear accelerators", "context_len": 36}}}, "pulsed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "The design of CEBAF allows the electron beam to be continuous rather than the pulsed beam typical of ring shaped accelerators", "context_len": 21}}}, "distinguishing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "One of the distinguishing features of JLab is the continuous nature of the electron beam , with a bunch length of less than 1 picosecond", "context_len": 25}}}, "niobium": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "Another is JLab 's use of superconducting RF ( SRF ) technology , which uses liquid helium to cool niobium to approximately 4 K ( 452", "context_len": 26}}}, "refrigerator": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 12, "context": "To achieve this , JLab uses the world 's largest liquid helium refrigerator , and was one of the first large-scale implementators of SRF technology", "context_len": 25}}}, "spectrometer": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 33, "context": "The Hanson Hall of Science 's facilities and resources include seven classrooms , thirty-five laboratories ( including a cadaver lab ) , a 400 MHz liquid-and solid-state NMR ( nuclear magnetic resonance ) spectrometer , scanning electron microscope , instrumentation for X-ray powder crystallography and a 40-foot greenhouse", "context_len": 48}}}, "converters": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "reconstruct": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "This digital data must be gathered and stored so that the physicist can later analyze the data and reconstruct the physics that occurred", "context_len": 23}}}, "concurrently": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Concurrently , an addition to the Test Lab , ( where the SRF cavities used in CEBAF and other accelerators used worldwide are manufactured ) is being constructed", "context_len": 28}}}, "tunable": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 18, "context": "`` The free-electron laser has the widest frequency range of any laser type , and can be widely tunable , currently ranging in wavelength from microwaves , through terahertz radiation and infrared , to the visible spectrum , to ultraviolet , to X-rays", "context_len": 43}}}, "kilowatts": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "JLab houses the world 's most powerful tunable free-electron laser , with an output of over 14 kilowatts", "context_len": 18}}}, "injection": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "The electrons are then captured and steered back to the injection end of the LINAC where they transfer most of their energy to a new batch of electrons to repeat the process", "context_len": 32}, "NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 8, "context": "The engine featured electronic ignition , electronic fuel injection , and stainless steel headers", "context_len": 14}}}, "digitized": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "In nuclear and particle physics experiments , the particle tracks are digitized by the data acquisition system , but the detectors are capable of generating a large number of possible measurements , or `` data channels ''", "context_len": 37}}}, "plugs": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 35, "context": "The ADC , TDC and other digital electronics are typically large circuit boards with connectors at the front edge that provide input and output for digital signals , and a connector at the back that plugs into a backplane", "context_len": 39}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "21st century equipment more often uses digital plugs , mainly by High-Definition Multimedia Interface", "context_len": 14}}}, "plugged": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "A group of boards are plugged into a chassis , or `` crate '' , that provides physical support , power and cooling for the boards and backplane", "context_len": 28}}}, "digitizing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "This arrangement allows electronics capable of digitizing many hundreds of channels to fit into a single chassis", "context_len": 17}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "This board , called a ReadOut Controller ( ROC ) , configures each of the digitizing boards upon first receiving data , reads the data from the digitizers , and formats the data for later analysis", "context_len": 36}}}, "configures": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "This board , called a ReadOut Controller ( ROC ) , configures each of the digitizing boards upon first receiving data , reads the data from the digitizers , and formats the data for later analysis", "context_len": 36}}}, "digitizers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "This board , called a ReadOut Controller ( ROC ) , configures each of the digitizing boards upon first receiving data , reads the data from the digitizers , and formats the data for later analysis", "context_len": 36}}}, "golding": {"freq": 9, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 9, "word_index": 0, "context": "Golding went on to write many more books , including `` The Inheritors '' , `` Rites of Passage '' and many others", "context_len": 23}}}, "schoolmaster": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "His father , Alec Golding , was a schoolmaster at Marlborough Grammar School", "context_len": 13}}}, "nostalgia": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "It has a similar meaning to the word `` nostalgia ''", "context_len": 11}}}, "pampered": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "It is about how much dependent you are on other people or your parents , how much pampered you are or how much difficult it is for you to be in a different place", "context_len": 34}}}, "homesick": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 4, "context": "Children may often feel homesick , especially when they are away from their parents for the first time", "context_len": 18}, "NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 4, "context": "People may easily feel homesick if they travel to an environment in which the culture is very difficult to what they are used to , and especially if a foreign language is being spoken", "context_len": 34}}}, "homesickness": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "Usually these feelings will go away as one gets used to the new environment , but sometimes homesickness can make a person depressed", "context_len": 23}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "A good way to help children overcome ( or avoid ) homesickness is to start with being away from home just for short periods , staying with people they know well , e", "context_len": 33}}}, "apprenticed": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 5, "context": "In 1768 , he was apprenticed to a local doctor , but he did not learn much from him", "context_len": 19}}}, "patience": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "She had the patience to wait until he had finished his medical studies before marrying him", "context_len": 16}}}, "perihelion": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "Their least distance from the Sun , their perihelion , is less than 1", "context_len": 14}}}, "meteoroids": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "They include more than ten thousand near-Earth asteroids ( NEAs ) , near-Earth comets , some solar-orbiting spacecraft , and meteoroids large enough to be tracked in space before striking the Earth", "context_len": 32}}}, "tracked": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "They include more than ten thousand near-Earth asteroids ( NEAs ) , near-Earth comets , some solar-orbiting spacecraft , and meteoroids large enough to be tracked in space before striking the Earth", "context_len": 32}}}, "meteors": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Most of these meteors explode harmlessly in the upper atmosphere", "context_len": 10}}}, "harmlessly": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "The freezing temperatures caused the gas to fall to the ground harmlessly", "context_len": 12}}}, "megatons": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "It released an energy of 10\u201315 megatons of TNT and destroyed roughly 2,000 square kilometres of forest", "context_len": 17}}}, "razed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Such an explosion , similar to one of the biggest nuclear weapons , could have razed London about as far out as the M25 ring road", "context_len": 26}}}, "flashlight": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "It is basically a super flashlight", "context_len": 6}}}, "diode": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Unlike gas , liquid , or solid-state lasers such as diode lasers , in which electrons are excited while bound to atoms , FELs use a relativistic electron beam as the lasing medium which moves freely through a magnetic structure , hence the term `` free electron", "context_len": 47}}}, "lasing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 31, "context": "Unlike gas , liquid , or solid-state lasers such as diode lasers , in which electrons are excited while bound to atoms , FELs use a relativistic electron beam as the lasing medium which moves freely through a magnetic structure , hence the term `` free electron", "context_len": 47}}}, "microwaves": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "`` The free-electron laser has the widest frequency range of any laser type , and can be widely tunable , currently ranging in wavelength from microwaves , through terahertz radiation and infrared , to the visible spectrum , to ultraviolet , to X-rays", "context_len": 43}}}, "terahertz": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 28, "context": "`` The free-electron laser has the widest frequency range of any laser type , and can be widely tunable , currently ranging in wavelength from microwaves , through terahertz radiation and infrared , to the visible spectrum , to ultraviolet , to X-rays", "context_len": 43}}}, "lieder": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 22, "context": "From the 1950s to the 1980s she was one of the best known classical music singers in opera , concert , and lieder", "context_len": 23}}}, "accompanist": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "She went to London in 1953 where she had singing lessons from Meriel St Clair and Helene Isepp , whose son Martin became her regular accompanist", "context_len": 26}}}, "oratorio": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 73, "context": "Among her best recordings are her singing of the Angel in Elgar 's `` The Dream of Gerontius '' , made with Sir John Barbirolli in December 1964 and Sir Simon Rattle over twenty years later ; her 1965 performances of Elgar 's `` Sea Pictures '' and Mahler 's R\u00fcckert-Lieder , also recorded with Barbirolli ; and , also from 1965 , the first commercial recording of Ralph Vaughan Williams 's Christmas oratorio `` Hodie '' under Sir David Willcocks", "context_len": 81}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "As well as opera , Janet Baker often sang oratorio roles and gave solo recitals", "context_len": 15}}}, "orchestrated": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "The first song to be orchestrated was `` L'Absence ''", "context_len": 10}}}, "prefectural": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "It is written in Engishiki Jinmyoutyou and the old status of a Shinto shrine is prefectural shrine", "context_len": 17}}}, "leftist": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "People say he has a `` philosophy unified by decentralism '' and as being `` a leader of the Neo-Luddites , '' , an `` anti-globalization leftist , '' and `` the theoretician for a new secessionist movement", "context_len": 38}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Sale worked initially in journalism for the leftist journal `` New Leader '' , `` a magazine founded in 1924 in part by socialists Norman Thomas and Eugene Debs , '' and the `` New York Times Magazine ''", "context_len": 39}}}, "secessionist": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 36, "context": "People say he has a `` philosophy unified by decentralism '' and as being `` a leader of the Neo-Luddites , '' , an `` anti-globalization leftist , '' and `` the theoretician for a new secessionist movement", "context_len": 38}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": null, "context": null, "context_len": 0}}}, "fraternizing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "Sale was one of the leaders of the May 23 , 1958 protest against university policies forbidding male and female students fraternizing and its `` in loco parentis '' policy", "context_len": 30}}}, "loco": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "Sale was one of the leaders of the May 23 , 1958 protest against university policies forbidding male and female students fraternizing and its `` in loco parentis '' policy", "context_len": 30}}}, "futuristic": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "In 1958 he collaborated with Thomas Pynchon on an unproduced futuristic musical called `` Minstrel Island", "context_len": 16}}}, "radicalism": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "The book `` is still considered one of the best sources on the youth activist organization that helped define 1960s radicalism", "context_len": 21}}}, "vowing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "`` In 1968 , he signed the Writers and Editors War Tax Protest pledge , vowing to refuse tax payments in protest against the Vietnam War", "context_len": 26}}}, "imperialist": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "In his 1990 book , `` The Conquest of Paradise : Christopher Columbus and the Columbian Legacy '' , Sale argued that Christopher Columbus was an imperialist bent on conquest from his first voyage", "context_len": 34}}}, "incompetent": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "Sale makes Columbus out to be cruel , greedy and incompetent ( even as a sailor ) , and a man who was perversely intent on abusing the natural paradise on which he intruded", "context_len": 34}}}, "perversely": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "Sale makes Columbus out to be cruel , greedy and incompetent ( even as a sailor ) , and a man who was perversely intent on abusing the natural paradise on which he intruded", "context_len": 34}}}, "intruded": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 33, "context": "Sale makes Columbus out to be cruel , greedy and incompetent ( even as a sailor ) , and a man who was perversely intent on abusing the natural paradise on which he intruded", "context_len": 34}}}, "courageous": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 36, "context": "In Mexico , it is known as `` R\u00edo Bravo '' or `` R\u00edo Bravo del Norte '' ; and the Spanish word `` bravo '' has many meanings , including `` brave '' , `` courageous '' , `` rough '' or `` wild '' , and `` Norte '' means `` North ''", "context_len": 55}}}, "skeptically": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Sale `` has written extensively and skeptically about technology , '' and has said he is `` a great admirer '' of anarchoprimitivist John Zerzan", "context_len": 25}}}, "merits": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 41, "context": "During promotion of his 1995 book `` Rebels Against the Future : The Luddites and Their War on the Industrial Revolution '' , Sale debated with `` Newsweek Magazine '' senior editor and technology columnist Steven Levy `` about the relative merits of the communications age ''", "context_len": 47}}}, "hovered": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "The bet was turned into a claim on the FX prediction market , where the probability has hovered around 25 %", "context_len": 21}}}, "godfathers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "Sale has been called `` one of the intellectual godfathers of the secessionist movement", "context_len": 14}}}, "secessionists": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 28, "context": "In 2006 , Middlebury sponsored the First North American Secessionist Convention , which attracted 40 participants from 16 secessionist organizations and was described as the first gathering of secessionists since the American Civil War", "context_len": 34}}}, "militaristic": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 22, "context": "`` He went on to say , `` If you want to leave a nation you think is corrupt , inefficient , militaristic , oppressive , repressive , but you do n't want to move to Canada or France , what do you do ? Well , the way is through secession , where you could stay home and be where you want to be", "context_len": 65}}}, "repressive": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "`` He went on to say , `` If you want to leave a nation you think is corrupt , inefficient , militaristic , oppressive , repressive , but you do n't want to move to Canada or France , what do you do ? Well , the way is through secession , where you could stay home and be where you want to be", "context_len": 65}}}, "totalling": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "On 1 July 2007 the RNZN had a total of 2,034 Regular Force personnel , 237 Naval Reserve personnel and 378 civilian employees , totalling 2,699", "context_len": 26}}}, "commissioning": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "She has responded to all of the major disasters in Australia and New Zealand since her commissioning", "context_len": 17}}}, "allotropes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "Graphene is the basic 2D ( two dimensional ) form of a number of 3D allotropes , such as graphite , charcoal , fullerene and carbon nanotubes", "context_len": 27}}}, "fullerene": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "Graphene is the basic 2D ( two dimensional ) form of a number of 3D allotropes , such as graphite , charcoal , fullerene and carbon nanotubes", "context_len": 27}}}, "honeycomb": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 4, "context": "Graphene is like a honeycomb or 'chicken wire ' structure , made of carbon atoms and their bonds", "context_len": 18}}}, "leaks": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "It slowly leaks even through a millimetre-thick window glass but our ultra-thin films completely block it", "context_len": 16}}}, "unimpeded": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "At the same time , water evaporates through them unimpeded", "context_len": 10}}}, "stranger": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Materials can not behave any stranger ''", "context_len": 7}}}, "electrolyte": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "There are 2 electrodes and an electrolyte solution to enable flow of charge", "context_len": 13}}}, "cathode": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "The difference is that one of the electrodes in graphene-based batteries , mostly the cathode , is replaced with a hybrid composite material ( solid-state metal graphene ) used in place of a standard solid-state metal", "context_len": 36}}}, "slimmer": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 9, "context": "This means that graphene would allow smartphones to be slimmer than ever and provide more space from additional electronics and allow to place higher capacity batteries", "context_len": 26}}}, "aiming": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "It gathers 16 of the best French schools , covering engineering science , management , architecture and veterinary , aiming to be of comparable status to the most famous universities of technology around the world", "context_len": 35}}}, "fianc\u00e9": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Rory began as Amy Pond 's fianc\u00e9", "context_len": 7}}}, "oddly": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "Mels secretly knows that she is their future daughter , Melody and is