e immune system will no longer detect them", "context_len": 23}}}, "intruder": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 19, "context": "When something gets past the skin , as through a cut , the immune cells work to find the intruder and to alert each other of the foreign object", "context_len": 29}}}, "intruders": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 17, "context": "Once a foreign cell or protein is detected , the immune system creates antibodies to fight the intruders , and sends special cells ( 'phagocytes ' ) to eat them up", "context_len": 31}}}, "antibodies": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "Once a foreign cell or protein is detected , the immune system creates antibodies to fight the intruders , and sends special cells ( 'phagocytes ' ) to eat them up", "context_len": 31}}}, "antimicrobial": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "These mechanisms include antimicrobial peptides ( called defensins ) , phagocytosis , and the complement system", "context_len": 16}}}, "mounts": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "The system mounts stronger attacks each time the pathogen is encountered", "context_len": 11}}}}